[{"category":"section","location":"reference/public/#Public-API-Reference","page":"Public API","text":"","title":"Public API Reference"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractBranchReductionTracker","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract anchor for the branch-reduction bookkeeping carried by a NetworkModel. The concrete tracker (and all reduction machinery) lives in the matrix-aware downstream package (POM), which constructs it during network model instantiation via set_reduced_branch_tracker!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractBranchReductionTracker"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractCostAtMinParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameters to define the cost at the minimum available power\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractCostAtMinParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractEvaluationData","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract type for runtime evaluator state stored inside the OptimizationContainer's EvaluationContainer.\n\nConcrete subtypes wrap whatever domain-specific data (power-flow solver state, exporter handles, etc.) the evaluator needs across iterations of calculate_aux_variables!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractEvaluationData"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractEvaluator","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract type for evaluator configurations attached to a NetworkModel.\n\nAn AbstractEvaluator is stateless configuration that, when used to build an OptimizationContainer, produces an AbstractEvaluationData (its runtime counterpart) via initialize_evaluation_data.\n\nConcrete subtypes (e.g. PowerFlowEvaluationModel) are defined in downstream packages such as PowerOperationsModels and its PowerFlows extension.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractEvaluator"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractEventModel","page":"Public API","text":"Abstracts for event contingencies\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractEventModel"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractNetworkData","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract anchor for the network artifacts a build derives from an AbstractNetworkSource: the reduction data plus whichever matrices the network formulation needs. Concrete containers live in POM.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractNetworkData"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractNetworkModel","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract supertype for network model formulations; neutral anchor for NetworkModel{T}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractNetworkModel"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractNetworkSource","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract anchor for the declaration of which network a NetworkModel is built on and how it is reduced. Concrete sources (a reduction specification, a prebuilt matrix, a prebuilt factorization core) live in the matrix-aware downstream package (POM), so IOM carries no dependency on any matrix implementation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractNetworkSource"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractOptimizationModel","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract supertype for DecisionModel and EmulationModel. Concrete subtypes are parameterized with an AbstractOptimizationProblem subtype.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractOptimizationModel"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractOptimizationProblem","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract type for any optimization problem. Concrete subtypes are provided by downstream domain libraries (e.g. PowerOperationsModels). DecisionModel{M} and EmulationModel{M} are parameterized over this type so any optimization problem can be wrapped without IOM knowing its domain.\n\nExample\n\nimport InfrastructureOptimizationModels const IOM = InfrastructureOptimizationModels struct MyCustomProblem <: IOM.AbstractOptimizationProblem end\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractOptimizationProblem"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockOffer","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract type for piecewise linear block offer variables\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockOffer"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockOfferConstraint","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract type for piecewise linear block offer constraints\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockOfferConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockWidthConstraint","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract type for piecewise linear block width constraints\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockWidthConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameters to define the breakpoints of a piecewise linear function\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameters to define the slopes of a piecewise linear cost function\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BoundDirection","page":"Public API","text":"Abstract type for bound direction. Used to unify upper/lower bound logic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BoundDirection"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModel-Union{Tuple{M}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Settings}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Settings, Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}}} where M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem","page":"Public API","text":"DecisionModel{M}(\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::IS.InfrastructureSystemsContainer,\n    settings::Settings,\n    jump_model::Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}=nothing;\n    name = nothing) where {M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem}\n\nSettings-taking constructor — builds the OptimizationContainer, finalizes the template, and validates time series. Both finalize_template! and validate_time_series! are extension points: downstream packages provide methods for their concrete AbstractProblemTemplate and model types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModel"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModel-Union{Tuple{M}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}}} where M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem","page":"Public API","text":"DecisionModel{M}(\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::IS.InfrastructureSystemsContainer,\n    jump_model::Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}=nothing;\n    kwargs...) where {M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem}\n\nKwargs constructor — accepts horizon/resolution/interval and all the standard solver/model settings, builds a Settings, and delegates to the settings-taking constructor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModel"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModel-Union{Tuple{M}, Tuple{Type{M}, AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}, Tuple{Type{M}, AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}}} where M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem","page":"Public API","text":"DecisionModel(\n    ::Type{M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem},\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer;\n    ...\n)\nDecisionModel(\n    ::Type{M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem},\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer,\n    jump_model::Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model};\n    kwargs...\n)\n\n\nDecisionModel(::Type{M}, template, sys, jump_model=nothing; kwargs...)\n    where {M <: AbstractOptimizationProblem}\n\nType-first dispatch variant.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModel"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecrementalCostAtMinParameter","page":"Public API","text":"AbstractCostAtMinParameter for the decremental case (power sink)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecrementalCostAtMinParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecrementalPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter","page":"Public API","text":"AbstractPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter for the decremental case (power sink)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecrementalPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecrementalPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter","page":"Public API","text":"AbstractPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter for the decremental case (power sink)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecrementalPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DefaultNetworkSource","page":"Public API","text":"Source used when a NetworkModel is constructed without an explicit one: build the network from the system with no reductions applied.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DefaultNetworkSource"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DeviceModel","page":"Public API","text":"DeviceModel(\n    ::Type{D},\n    ::Type{B};\n    feedforwards = Vector{AbstractAffectFeedforward}(),\n    use_slacks = false,\n    duals = Vector{DataType}(),\n    time_series_names = get_default_time_series_names(D, B),\n    attributes = Dict{String, Any}(),\n    outages = IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent[],\n)\n\nEstablishes the model for a particular device specified by type. Uses the keyword argument feedforwards to enable passing values between operation models at simulation time.\n\nArguments\n\n::Type{D}: Device Type (e.g., PSY.ThermalStandard or a mock device type)\n::Type{B} where B<:AbstractDeviceFormulation: Abstract Device Formulation\nfeedforwards::Vector{<:AbstractAffectFeedforward} = Vector{AbstractAffectFeedforward}() : use to pass parameters between models\nuse_slacks::Bool = false : Add slacks to the device model. Implementation is model dependent and not all models feature slacks\nduals::Vector{DataType} = Vector{DataType}(): use to pass constraint type to calculate the duals. The DataType needs to be a valid ConstraintType\ntime_series_names::Dict{Type{<:TimeSeriesParameter}, String} = get_default_time_series_names(D, B) : use to specify time series names associated to the device`\nattributes::Dict{String, Any} = get_default_attributes(D, B) : use to specify attributes to the device\noutages::AbstractVector{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent} = IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent[] : N-1 contingencies to model when the formulation is security-constrained. The constructor stores the IS.get_id(outage) of each entry as a key in the model's outages::Dict{Int, Dict{DataType, Set{String}}} field with empty inner maps; template validation in downstream packages fills the inner maps with the per-type set of monitored component names that each outage carries. Power-specific validation (e.g. checking that entries are PSY.Outage subtypes) lives in PowerOperationsModels. If B is not security-constrained, a non-empty value is dropped with a warning.\n\nExample\n\nthermal_gens = DeviceModel(ThermalStandard, ThermalBasicUnitCommitment)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DeviceModel"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModel-Union{Tuple{M}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Settings}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Settings, Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}}} where M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem","page":"Public API","text":"EmulationModel{M}(\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::IS.InfrastructureSystemsContainer,\n    settings::Settings,\n    jump_model::Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}=nothing;\n    name = nothing) where {M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem}\n\nSettings-taking constructor — finalizes the template, builds the OptimizationContainer with single-time-series data, and validates time series. Both finalize_template! and validate_time_series! are extension points implemented by downstream packages for their concrete template/model types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModel"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModel-Union{Tuple{M}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}, Tuple{AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}}} where M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem","page":"Public API","text":"EmulationModel{M}(\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::IS.InfrastructureSystemsContainer,\n    jump_model::Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}=nothing;\n    kwargs...) where {M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem}\n\nKwargs constructor — builds a Settings (with horizon == resolution, since emulation models solve one step at a time) and delegates to the Settings-taking constructor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModel"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModel-Union{Tuple{M}, Tuple{Type{M}, AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}, Tuple{Type{M}, AbstractProblemTemplate, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer, Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model}}} where M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem","page":"Public API","text":"EmulationModel(\n    ::Type{M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem},\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer;\n    ...\n)\nEmulationModel(\n    ::Type{M<:AbstractOptimizationProblem},\n    template::AbstractProblemTemplate,\n    sys::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer,\n    jump_model::Union{Nothing, JuMP.Model};\n    kwargs...\n)\n\n\nEmulationModel(::Type{M}, template, sys, jump_model=nothing; kwargs...)\n    where {M <: AbstractOptimizationProblem}\n\nType-first dispatch variant.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModel"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModelStore","page":"Public API","text":"Stores outputs data for one EmulationModel. Parameterized by T <: AbstractDataset to support different storage backends (e.g., InMemoryDataset, HDF5Dataset).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EmulationModelStore"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EvaluationContainer","page":"Public API","text":"Holds the evaluators registered on a NetworkModel and their associated runtime data, keyed by concrete evaluator type.\n\nevaluators is populated by the user when constructing a NetworkModel; evaluation_data is populated during OptimizationContainer construction by calling initialize_evaluation_data for each registered evaluator.\n\nThe split between the two dictionaries may evolve; for now we keep them as parallel keyed dictionaries so that evaluation_data[T] is the runtime state produced from evaluators[T].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EvaluationContainer"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.FixValueParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameter to fix a variable value (e.g., from feedforward).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.FixValueParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.FixedOutput","page":"Public API","text":"Formulation type to augment the power balance constraint expression with a time series parameter\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.FixedOutput"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.FuelCostParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameter to define fuel cost time series\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.FuelCostParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IncrementalCostAtMinParameter","page":"Public API","text":"AbstractCostAtMinParameter for the incremental case (power source)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IncrementalCostAtMinParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IncrementalPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter","page":"Public API","text":"AbstractPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter for the incremental case (power source)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IncrementalPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IncrementalPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter","page":"Public API","text":"AbstractPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter for the incremental case (power source)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IncrementalPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InitialCondition","page":"Public API","text":"Container for the initial condition data\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InitialCondition"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InitialConditionsData","page":"Public API","text":"Stores data to populate initial conditions before the build call\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InitialConditionsData"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NetworkModel","page":"Public API","text":"Establishes the NetworkModel for a given AC network formulation type.\n\nArguments\n\n::Type{T} where T <: AbstractNetworkModel: the network formulation type.\n\nAccepted keyword arguments\n\nuse_slacks::Bool = false   Adds slack buses to the network modeling.\nnetwork_source::AbstractNetworkSource = DefaultNetworkSource()   Declares which network the model is built on and how it is reduced. The default   builds it from the system with no reductions. Concrete sources (a reduction   specification, a prebuilt matrix, a prebuilt factorization core) live in the   matrix-aware downstream package.\nreduction_exceptions::Vector{Int} = Int[]   Bus numbers the reduction must not eliminate, on top of those the template   itself pins.\nduals::Vector{DataType} = Vector{DataType}()   Constraint types for which duals should be recorded.\nevaluations::EvaluationContainer   External evaluators (e.g. power-flow) keyed by concrete evaluator type.   Default is an empty container — no evaluator runs.\n\nNotes\n\nnetwork_data holds every matrix and the reduction data derived from network_source during instantiate_network_model!; it is nothing before then.\nsubnetworks, modeled_branch_types and reduced_branch_tracker are internal fields managed by the model.\nsubsystem can be set after construction via set_subsystem!(model, id).\n\nExamples (concrete types like PTDFPowerModel, CopperPlatePowerModel are defined in PowerSimulations)\n\nec = EvaluationContainer()\n\nadd_evaluator!(ec, PFS.PowerFlowEvaluationModel, PFS.PowerFlowEvaluationModel())\n\nnw = NetworkModel(PTDFPowerModel;\n\nnetwork_source = NetworkReductionSpec(RadialReduction()),\n\nevaluations = ec)\n\n\n\nnw2 = NetworkModel(CopperPlatePowerModel)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NetworkModel"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OnStatusParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameter to define unit commitment status updated from the system state\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OnStatusParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationModelExportFormatModule.OptimizationModelExportFormat","page":"Public API","text":"Format used to export the optimization model to disk on each solve.\n\nValues\n\nNONE: Do not export the model.\nLP: Export to the LP file format (.lp).\nMOF: Export to MathOptFormat (.json).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationModelExportFormatModule.OptimizationModelExportFormat"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs","page":"Public API","text":"mutable struct OptimizationProblemOutputs <: Outputs\n\nContainer for the outputs of an optimization problem, including variable values, dual values, parameter values, expression values, and optimizer statistics.\n\nThis type stores all output data from solving an optimization problem and provides methods to read, export, and serialize the outputs. Instead of accessing the output dictionary fields directly, use the read_foo functions.\n\nFields\n\nbase_power::Float64: Base power used for per-unit conversion\ntimestamps::Vector{Dates.DateTime}: Time stamps for each step in the outputs\nsource_data::Union{Nothing, InfrastructureSystemsType}: Reference to the source data (e.g., system)\nsource_data_uuid::Base.UUID: UUID of the source data for validation. Internal usage.\naux_variable_values::Dict{AuxVarKey, DataFrame}: Auxiliary variable outputs. See read_aux_variable and read_aux_variables\nvariable_values::Dict{VariableKey, DataFrame}: Decision variable outputs. See read_variable and read_variables\ndual_values::Dict{ConstraintKey, DataFrame}: Dual outputs. See read_dual and read_duals\nparameter_values::Dict{ParameterKey, DataFrame}: Parameter outputs. See read_parameter and read_parameters\nexpression_values::Dict{ExpressionKey, DataFrame}: Expression outputs. See read_expression and read_expressions\noptimizer_stats::DataFrame: Optimizer statistics for each solve\noptimization_container_metadata::OptimizationContainerMetadata: Metadata about the optimization container. Internal usage.\nmodel_type::String: Type of optimization model. Internal usage.\noutputs_dir::String: Directory where outputs are stored\noutput_dir::String: Directory for exported output\n\nSee also: OptimizerStats, OptimizationProblemOutputsExport\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Public API","text":"OptimizationProblemOutputs(directory::AbstractString) -> Any\n\n\nConstruct a OptimizationProblemOutputs instance from a serialized directory. It is up to the user or a higher-level package to set the source data using set_source_data!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs-Tuple{DecisionModel}","page":"Public API","text":"OptimizationProblemOutputs(model::DecisionModel)\n\n\nConstruct OptimizationProblemOutputs from a solved DecisionModel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs-Tuple{EmulationModel}","page":"Public API","text":"OptimizationProblemOutputs(model::EmulationModel)\n\n\nConstruct OptimizationProblemOutputs from a solved EmulationModel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputs"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputsExport","page":"Public API","text":"struct OptimizationProblemOutputsExport\n\nConfiguration for exporting optimization problem outputs to files.\n\nSpecifies which variables, duals, parameters, expressions, and auxiliary variables should be exported when calling export_outputs on an OptimizationProblemOutputs instance.\n\nFields\n\nname::Symbol: Name identifier for this export configuration\nduals::Set{ConstraintKey}: Specific dual values to export\nexpressions::Set{ExpressionKey}: Specific expression values to export\nparameters::Set{ParameterKey}: Specific parameter values to export\nvariables::Set{VariableKey}: Specific variable values to export\naux_variables::Set{AuxVarKey}: Specific auxiliary variable values to export\noptimizer_stats::Bool: Whether to export optimizer statistics\nstore_all_flags::Dict{Symbol, Bool}: Flags indicating whether to export all values of each type (e.g., all variables, all duals). Set via constructor keyword arguments like store_all_variables = true. When a flag is true, all values of that type are exported regardless of what specific keys are passed in the corresponding set.\n\nExample\n\nexport_config = OptimizationProblemOutputsExport(\n    \"MyExport\";\n    store_all_variables = true,\n    store_all_duals = false,\n    optimizer_stats = true,\n)\nexport_outputs(outputs, export_config)\n\nSee also: OptimizationProblemOutputs, export_outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizationProblemOutputsExport"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizerStats","page":"Public API","text":"mutable struct OptimizerStats\n\nStatistics and performance metrics from an optimization solver run.\n\nCaptures solver-reported metrics (termination status, objective value, solve time) as well as timing information for auxiliary computations. Fields marked as Union{Missing, T} may not be available for all solvers.\n\nFields\n\ndetailed_stats::Bool: Whether detailed statistics are available\nobjective_value::Float64: Optimal objective function value\ntermination_status::Int: Solver termination status code\nprimal_status::Int: Status of the primal solution\ndual_status::Int: Status of the dual solution\nsolver_solve_time::Float64: Time reported by the solver for the solve\nresult_count::Int: Number of solutions found\nhas_values::Bool: Whether primal values are available\nhas_duals::Bool: Whether dual values are available\nobjective_bound::Union{Missing, Float64}: Bound on the objective (for MIP solvers)\nrelative_gap::Union{Missing, Float64}: Relative optimality gap (for MIP solvers)\ndual_objective_value::Union{Missing, Float64}: Dual objective value\nsolve_time::Float64: Total solve time\nbarrier_iterations::Union{Missing, Int}: Number of barrier iterations\nsimplex_iterations::Union{Missing, Int}: Number of simplex iterations\nnode_count::Union{Missing, Int}: Number of branch-and-bound nodes explored\ntimed_solve_time::Float64: Externally timed solve duration\ntimed_calculate_aux_variables::Float64: Time to calculate auxiliary variables\ntimed_calculate_dual_variables::Float64: Time to calculate dual variables\nsolve_bytes_alloc::Union{Missing, Float64}: Memory allocated during solve\nsec_in_gc::Union{Missing, Float64}: Time spent in garbage collection\n\nSee also: OptimizationProblemOutputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizerStats"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizerStats-Tuple{Vector{Float64}}","page":"Public API","text":"OptimizerStats(data::Vector{Float64}) -> OptimizerStats\n\n\nConstruct OptimizerStats from a vector that was serialized.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OptimizerStats"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOffer","page":"Public API","text":"Struct to dispatch the creation of piecewise linear block decremental offer variables for objective function\n\nDocs abbreviation: delta_d\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOffer"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOfferConstraint","page":"Public API","text":"Struct to create the PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOfferConstraint associated with a specified variable.\n\nSee the piecewise linear cost functions section for more information.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOfferConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalWidthConstraint","page":"Public API","text":"Struct to create the block-width limit associated with a piecewise-linear decremental offer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalWidthConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOffer","page":"Public API","text":"Struct to dispatch the creation of piecewise linear block incremental offer variables for objective function\n\nDocs abbreviation: delta\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOffer"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOfferConstraint","page":"Public API","text":"Struct to create the PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOfferConstraint associated with a specified variable.\n\nSee the piecewise linear cost functions section for more information.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOfferConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalWidthConstraint","page":"Public API","text":"Struct to create the block-width limit associated with a piecewise-linear incremental offer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalWidthConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearCostVariable","page":"Public API","text":"Lambda weight variables lambda_i in 0 1 for the convex-combination PWL cost formulation.\n\nEach breakpoint of a [IS.PiecewisePointCurve] gets one lambda variable per component per time step. The operating point and cost are expressed as weighted averages of breakpoint values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearCostVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ServiceModel","page":"Public API","text":"Establishes the model for all services of a particular type. A ServiceModel represents every service of its type in the system. Uses the keyword argument feedforwards to enable passing values between operation models at simulation time.\n\nArguments\n\n-::Type{D}: Power System Service Type -::Type{B}: Abstract Service Formulation\n\nAccepted Key Words\n\nfeedforwards::Vector{<:AbstractAffectFeedforward} : use to pass parameters between models\n\nExample\n\nreserves = ServiceModel(PSY.VariableReserve{PSY.ReserveUp}, RangeReserve)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ServiceModel"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ShutdownCostParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameter to define shutdown cost time series\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ShutdownCostParameter"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.StartupCostParameter","page":"Public API","text":"Parameter to define startup cost time series\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.StartupCostParameter"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_generic_incremental_interpolation_constraint!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{S}, Tuple{R}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{R}, Type{S}, Type{T}, Type{U}, Type{V}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{W}, Vector{W}}, Dict{String, Vector{Float64}}, Dict{String, Vector{Float64}}}} where {R<:VariableType, S<:VariableType, T<:VariableType, U<:VariableType, V<:ConstraintType, W<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"_add_generic_incremental_interpolation_constraint!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{R<:VariableType},\n    ::Type{S<:VariableType},\n    ::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    ::Type{U<:VariableType},\n    ::Type{V<:ConstraintType},\n    devices::Union{Array{W<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{W<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    dic_var_bkpts::Dict{String, Vector{Float64}},\n    dic_function_bkpts::Dict{String, Vector{Float64}};\n    meta\n)\n\n\n_add_generic_incremental_interpolation_constraint!(container, ::R, ::S, ::T, ::U, ::V, devices, dic_var_bkpts, dic_function_bkpts; meta)\n\nAdd incremental piecewise linear interpolation constraints to an optimization container.\n\nThis function implements the incremental method for piecewise linear approximation in optimization models. It creates constraints that relate the original variable (x) to its piecewise linear approximation (y = f(x)) using interpolation variables (δ) and binary variables (z) to ensure proper ordering.\n\nThe incremental method represents each segment of the PWL function as:\n\nx = x₁ + Σᵢ δᵢ(xᵢ₊₁ - xᵢ) where δᵢ ∈ [0,1]\ny = y₁ + Σᵢ δᵢ(yᵢ₊₁ - yᵢ) where yᵢ = f(xᵢ)\n\nBinary variables z ensure the incremental property: δᵢ₊₁ ≤ zᵢ ≤ δᵢ for adjacent segments.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: The optimization container to add constraints to\n::R: Type parameter for the original variable (x)\n::S: Type parameter for the approximated variable (y = f(x))\n::T: Type parameter for the interpolation variables (δ)\n::U: Type parameter for the binary interpolation variables (z)\n::V: Type parameter for the constraint type\ndevices::Union{Vector{W}, IS.FlattenIteratorWrapper{W}}: Collection of devices to apply constraints to\ndic_var_bkpts::Dict{String, Vector{Float64}}: Breakpoints in the domain (x-coordinates) for each device\ndic_function_bkpts::Dict{String, Vector{Float64}}: Function values at breakpoints (y-coordinates) for each device\nmeta: Metadata for constraint naming (default: empty)\n\nType Parameters\n\nR <: VariableType: Original variable type\nS <: VariableType: Approximated variable type\nT <: VariableType: Interpolation variable type\nU <: VariableType: Binary interpolation variable type\nV <: ConstraintType: Constraint type\nW <: IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent: Component type for devices\n\nNotes\n\nCreates two types of constraints: variable interpolation and function interpolation\nAdds ordering constraints for binary variables to ensure incremental property\nAll constraints are applied for each device and time step\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_generic_incremental_interpolation_constraint!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_breakpoints_for_pwl_function-Tuple{Float64, Float64, Any}","page":"Public API","text":"_get_breakpoints_for_pwl_function(\n    min_val::Float64,\n    max_val::Float64,\n    f;\n    num_segments\n) -> Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Vector{Float64}}\n\n\n_get_breakpoints_for_pwl_function(min_val, max_val, f; num_segments = DEFAULT_INTERPOLATION_LENGTH)\n\nGenerate breakpoints for piecewise linear (PWL) approximation of a nonlinear function.\n\nThis function creates equally-spaced breakpoints over the specified domain [minval, maxval] and evaluates the given function at each breakpoint to construct a piecewise linear approximation. The breakpoints are used in optimization problems to linearize nonlinear constraints or objectives.\n\nArguments\n\nmin_val::Float64: Minimum value of the domain for the PWL approximation\nmax_val::Float64: Maximum value of the domain for the PWL approximation\nf: Function to be approximated (must be callable with Float64 input)\nnum_segments::Int: Number of linear segments in the PWL approximation (default: DEFAULTINTERPOLATIONLENGTH)\n\nReturns\n\nTuple{Vector{Float64}, Vector{Float64}}: A tuple containing:\nx_bkpts: Vector of x-coordinates (breakpoints) in the domain\ny_bkpts: Vector of y-coordinates (function values at breakpoints)\n\nNotes\n\nThe number of breakpoints is num_segments + 1\nBreakpoints are equally spaced across the domain\nThe first breakpoint is always at min_val and the last at max_val\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_breakpoints_for_pwl_function"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_constant_to_jump_expression!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, Float64}} where T<:JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar","page":"Public API","text":"add_constant_to_jump_expression!(\n    expression::JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar,\n    value::Float64\n)\n\n\nAdd constant value to JuMP expression.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_constant_to_jump_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_function_parameter_container!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Tuple{Vararg{Type}}, Vararg{Any}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.ObjectiveFunctionParameter, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_cost_function_parameter_container!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.ObjectiveFunctionParameter},\n    ::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    variable_types::Tuple{Vararg{Type}},\n    axs...;\n    sos_variable,\n    uses_compact_power,\n    data_type,\n    sparse,\n    meta\n) -> ParameterContainer{T, U, CostFunctionAttributes{Float64}} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:AbstractArray}\n\n\nAllocate a cost-function parameter container (CostFunctionAttributes).\n\nNote that data_type sets both the attributes' type parameter and the parameter array's element type, bypassing get_param_eltype(container).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_function_parameter_container!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_invariant!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{E}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, Float64, Type{E}, Type{C}, String, Int64}} where {E<:ExpressionType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_cost_term_invariant!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    quantity::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    rate::Float64,\n    _::Type{E<:ExpressionType},\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nAdd cost term to expression and invariant objective.\n\nComputes cost = quantity * rate, adds to target expression (if present), propagates to ProductionCostExpression (when applicable), and adds to the time-invariant part of the objective.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nquantity: the value being costed (e.g., variable value, expression value)\nrate: scalar cost rate (e.g., /MWh, /MMBTU)\nE: target expression type (caller provides, e.g., ProductionCostExpression)\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_invariant!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_to_expression!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{E}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, Float64, Type{E}, Type{C}, String, Int64}} where {E<:ExpressionType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_cost_term_to_expression!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    quantity::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    rate::Float64,\n    _::Type{E<:ExpressionType},\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nAdd cost term to a target expression (no objective hook).\n\nComputes cost = quantity * rate, adds it to expression E for component C at time t if that expression exists, and propagates into ProductionCostExpression when E <: ConstituentCostExpression. Use this when the caller wants to record the cost in an expression container without adding to the JuMP objective (e.g., fuel consumption, where the term is a downstream quantity rather than a cost that should be minimized).\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nquantity: the value being costed (e.g., variable value, expression value)\nrate: scalar cost rate (e.g., /MWh, /MMBTU)\nE: target expression type (caller provides)\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_to_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_variant!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{E}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, Float64, Type{E}, Type{C}, String, Int64}} where {E<:ExpressionType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_cost_term_variant!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    quantity::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    rate::Float64,\n    _::Type{E<:ExpressionType},\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nAdd cost term to expression and variant objective with explicit rate.\n\nLike add_cost_term_invariant! but adds to variant objective. Use when the rate is computed at runtime rather than looked up from parameters.\n\nNote: the variant/invariant split is about whether the objective expression gets rebuilt between simulation steps, not about parameter references. Variant terms are regenerated each step; invariant terms stay constant.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nquantity: the value being costed (e.g., variable value, expression value)\nrate: scalar cost rate (e.g., /MWh)\nE: target expression type (caller provides, e.g., ProductionCostExpression)\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_variant!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_variant!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{E}, Tuple{P}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, Type{P}, Type{E}, Type{C}, String, Int64}} where {P<:ParameterType, E<:ExpressionType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_cost_term_variant!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    quantity::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    _::Type{P<:ParameterType},\n    _::Type{E<:ExpressionType},\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64\n) -> Any\n\n\nAdd cost term to expression and variant objective.\n\nFetches rate from parameter, computes cost = quantity * rate, adds to target expression (if present), and adds to the time-variant part of the objective.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nquantity: the value being costed (e.g., variable value, expression value)\nP: parameter type for the rate (caller provides, e.g., FuelCostParameter)\nE: target expression type (caller provides, e.g., ProductionCostExpression)\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_term_variant!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_to_expression!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{S}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{S}, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, Type{T}, String, Int64}} where {S<:Union{FuelConsumptionExpression, CostExpressions}, T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_cost_to_expression!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{S<:Union{FuelConsumptionExpression, CostExpressions}},\n    cost_expression::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    component_name::String,\n    time_period::Int64\n)\n\n\nAdd a cost expression term to a cost-related expression container.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_cost_to_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_event_parameter_container!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Type{V}, Vararg{Any}}} where {T<:EventParameter, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:InfrastructureSystems.SupplementalAttribute}","page":"Public API","text":"add_event_parameter_container!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:EventParameter},\n    ::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    ::Type{V<:InfrastructureSystems.SupplementalAttribute},\n    axs...;\n    sparse,\n    meta\n) -> Union{ParameterContainer{T, U, A} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray, A<:(EventParametersAttributes{V, T} where {V<:InfrastructureSystems.SupplementalAttribute, T<:EventParameter})}, ParameterContainer{T, U, A} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:(JuMP.Containers.SparseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N), A<:(EventParametersAttributes{V, T} where {V<:InfrastructureSystems.SupplementalAttribute, T<:EventParameter})}}\n\n\nAllocate an event parameter container (EventParametersAttributes). U is the component type the event affects; V is the supplemental-attribute type describing the event itself.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_event_parameter_container!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_linear_ramp_constraints!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{S}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{<:ConstraintType}, Type{S}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Type{<:AbstractNetworkModel}}} where {S<:Union{ActivePowerVariable, PowerAboveMinimumVariable}, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"add_linear_ramp_constraints!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    T::Type{<:ConstraintType},\n    U::Type{S<:Union{ActivePowerVariable, PowerAboveMinimumVariable}},\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    _::Type{<:AbstractNetworkModel}\n)\n\n\nConstructs allowed rate-of-change constraints from variables, initial condtions, and rate data.\n\nIf t = 1:\n\nvariable[name, 1] - initial_conditions[ix].value <= rate_data[1][ix].up\n\ninitial_conditions[ix].value - variable[name, 1] <= rate_data[1][ix].down\n\nIf t > 1:\n\nvariable[name, t] - variable[name, t-1] <= rate_data[1][ix].up\n\nvariable[name, t-1] - variable[name, t] <= rate_data[1][ix].down\n\nLaTeX\n\nr^down leq x_1 - x_init leq r^up text for  t = 1\n\nr^down leq x_t - x_t-1 leq r^up forall t geq 2\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_linear_ramp_constraints!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_linear_to_jump_expression!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, JuMP.VariableRef, Float64, Float64}} where T<:JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar","page":"Public API","text":"add_linear_to_jump_expression!(\n    expression::JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar,\n    var::JuMP.VariableRef,\n    multiplier::Float64,\n    constant::Float64\n)\n\n\nAdd affine term to JuMP expression: expression += constant + multiplier * var\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_linear_to_jump_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_param_container_shared_axes!-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, ParameterKey, ParameterAttributes, DataType, Vararg{Any, N}}} where N","page":"Public API","text":"add_param_container_shared_axes!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    key::ParameterKey,\n    attribute::ParameterAttributes,\n    param_type::DataType,\n    axs...;\n    sparse\n) -> Union{ParameterContainer{T, U} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray}, ParameterContainer{T, U} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:(JuMP.Containers.SparseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N)}}\n\n\nAllocate a parameter container where param and multiplier arrays share the same axes. Covers VariableValue, Event, CostFunction parameter types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_param_container_shared_axes!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_param_container_split_axes!-Tuple{OptimizationContainer, ParameterKey, ParameterAttributes, DataType, Any, Any, Any, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"Public API","text":"add_param_container_split_axes!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    key::ParameterKey,\n    attribute::ParameterAttributes,\n    param_type::DataType,\n    param_axs,\n    multiplier_axs,\n    additional_axs,\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64};\n    sparse\n) -> Union{ParameterContainer{T, U} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray}, ParameterContainer{T, U} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:(JuMP.Containers.SparseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N)}}\n\n\nAllocate a parameter container where param and multiplier arrays have different axes. Used for time series parameters where paramaxs and multiplieraxs may differ.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_param_container_split_axes!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_parameterized_lower_bound_range_constraints-Union{Tuple{X}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{P}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Type{P}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Type{X}}} where {T<:ConstraintType, U<:Union{ExpressionType, VariableType}, P<:ParameterType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, X<:AbstractNetworkModel}","page":"Public API","text":"add_parameterized_lower_bound_range_constraints(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{U<:Union{ExpressionType, VariableType}},\n    _::Type{P<:ParameterType},\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    _::Type{X<:AbstractNetworkModel}\n)\n\n\nAdd array[name, t] >= rhs[name, t] constraints of type T, where array is the variable or expression U and the right-hand side is built from the parameter P. The right-hand side depends on the parameter family:\n\ngeneric P: multiplier[name, t] * parameter[name, t]\nP <: EventParameter: get_max_active_power(device) * parameter[name, t]\nP <: TimeSeriesParameter: multiplier[name, t] * parameter_column[t], and only devices that own the time series named in get_time_series_names(model)[P] are constrained.\n\nMirror of add_parameterized_upper_bound_range_constraints.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_parameterized_lower_bound_range_constraints"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_parameterized_upper_bound_range_constraints-Union{Tuple{X}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{P}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Type{P}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Type{X}}} where {T<:ConstraintType, U<:Union{ExpressionType, VariableType}, P<:ParameterType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, X<:AbstractNetworkModel}","page":"Public API","text":"add_parameterized_upper_bound_range_constraints(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{U<:Union{ExpressionType, VariableType}},\n    _::Type{P<:ParameterType},\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    _::Type{X<:AbstractNetworkModel}\n)\n\n\nAdd array[name, t] <= rhs[name, t] constraints of type T, where array is the variable or expression U and the right-hand side is built from the parameter P. The right-hand side depends on the parameter family:\n\ngeneric P: multiplier[name, t] * parameter[name, t]\nP <: EventParameter: get_max_active_power(device) * parameter[name, t]\nP <: TimeSeriesParameter: multiplier[name, t] * parameter_column[t], and only devices that own the time series named in get_time_series_names(model)[P] are constrained.\n\nMirror of add_parameterized_lower_bound_range_constraints.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_parameterized_upper_bound_range_constraints"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_to_jump_expression!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, Float64, Float64}} where T<:JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar","page":"Public API","text":"add_proportional_to_jump_expression!(\n    expression::JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar,\n    parameter::Float64,\n    multiplier::Float64\n)\n\n\nAdd product of parameter and multiplier to JuMP expression: expression += parameter * multiplier\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_to_jump_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_to_jump_expression!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, U, Float64}} where {T<:JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar, U<:JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}","page":"Public API","text":"add_proportional_to_jump_expression!(\n    expression::JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar,\n    var::JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar,\n    multiplier::Float64\n)\n\n\nAdd variable with multiplier to JuMP expression: expression += multiplier * var\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_to_jump_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_constraint_delta!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, T, Type{U}, Type{D}, Vector{<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}}, Vector{JuMP.VariableRef}, Int64, Type{W}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, U<:VariableType, D, W<:AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockOfferConstraint}","page":"Public API","text":"add_pwl_constraint_delta!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    ::Type{U<:VariableType},\n    ::Type{D},\n    break_points::Vector{<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}},\n    pwl_vars::Vector{JuMP.VariableRef},\n    period::Int64,\n    ::Type{W<:AbstractPiecewiseLinearBlockOfferConstraint};\n    meta\n)\n\n\nImplement the constraints for PWL Block Offer variables. That is:\n\nsum_kinmathcalK delta_kt = p_t \nsum_kinmathcalK delta_kt leq P_k+1t^max - P_kt^max\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_constraint_delta!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_linking_constraint!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{K}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{K}, Type{C}, String, Int64, JuMP.VariableRef, Vector{JuMP.VariableRef}, Vector{Float64}}} where {K<:ConstraintType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_pwl_linking_constraint!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{K<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    power_var::JuMP.VariableRef,\n    pwl_vars::Vector{JuMP.VariableRef},\n    breakpoints::Vector{Float64}\n)\n\n\nAdd PWL linking constraint: power variable equals weighted sum of breakpoints.\n\nP[name, t] == Σ δ[i] * breakpoint[i]\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nK: constraint type (caller provides)\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\npower_var: the power variable to link (JuMP variable reference)\npwl_vars: vector of PWL delta variables\nbreakpoints: vector of breakpoint values (in p.u.)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_linking_constraint!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_normalization_constraint!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{K}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{K}, Type{C}, String, Int64, Vector{JuMP.VariableRef}, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}}} where {K<:ConstraintType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_pwl_normalization_constraint!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{K<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    pwl_vars::Vector{JuMP.VariableRef},\n    on_status::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}\n)\n\n\nAdd PWL normalization constraint: delta variables sum to on_status.\n\nΣ δ[i] == on_status\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nK: constraint type (caller provides)\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\npwl_vars: vector of PWL delta variables\non_status: the on/off status (1.0, or a JuMP variable/parameter)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_normalization_constraint!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_sos2_constraint!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, String, Int64, Vector{JuMP.VariableRef}}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Public API","text":"add_pwl_sos2_constraint!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    pwl_vars::Vector{JuMP.VariableRef}\n)\n\n\nAdd SOS2 constraint for PWL variables (required for non-convex curves).\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\npwl_vars: vector of PWL delta variables\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_sos2_constraint!"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_term_delta!","page":"Public API","text":"add_pwl_term_delta!(direction, container, component, cost_function, ::Type{VariableType}, ::Type{Formulation})\n\nAdd the delta PWL objective term for a static cost function. POM provides the method dispatching on PSY.OfferCurveCost.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_term_delta!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_term_lambda!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, T, Union{InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve}, InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve}}, Type{U}, Type{V}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, U<:VariableType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"add_pwl_term_lambda!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::Union{InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve}, InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve}},\n    _::Type{U<:VariableType},\n    _::Type{V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nAdd PWL cost terms using the lambda (convex combination) formulation.\n\nGiven a PiecewisePointCurve with breakpoints (P_i C_i), this function:\n\nCreates lambda variables lambda_i in 0 1 at each breakpoint via add_pwl_variables_lambda!.\nAdds linking and normalization constraints via _add_pwl_constraint_standard!.\nIf the cost curve is non-convex, adds an SOS2 adjacency constraint so that at most two neighboring lambda values are nonzero.\nBuilds the cost expression C = sum_i lambda_i  C(P_i).\n\nReturns a vector of cost expressions, one per time step, which the caller adds to the objective function.\n\nSee also: add_pwl_term_delta! for the delta (block-offer) formulation used by MarketBidCost.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_term_lambda!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_variables_delta!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{V}, Type{C}, String, Int64, Int64}} where {V<:SparseVariableType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"add_pwl_variables_delta!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{V<:SparseVariableType},\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    n_points::Int64;\n    upper_bound\n) -> Vector{JuMP.VariableRef}\n\n\nCreate PWL delta variables for a component at a given time period.\n\nCreates n_points variables with specified bounds.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nV: variable type for the delta variables (caller provides)\nC: component type\nname: component name\nt: time period\nn_points: number of PWL points (= number of delta variables)\nupper_bound: upper bound for variables (default 1.0; use Inf for block offer  formulation where segment capacity is enforced by constraints instead)\n\nReturns\n\nVector of the created JuMP variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_variables_delta!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_range_constraints!-Union{Tuple{X}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Type{X}}} where {T<:ConstraintType, U<:VariableType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, X<:AbstractNetworkModel}","page":"Public API","text":"add_range_constraints!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{U<:VariableType},\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    _::Type{X<:AbstractNetworkModel}\n)\n\n\nConstructs min/max range constraint from device variable.\n\nIf min and max within an epsilon width:\n\nvariable[name, t] == limits.max\n\nOtherwise:\n\nlimits.min <= variable[name, t] <= limits.max\n\nwhere limits in constraint_infos.\n\nLaTeX\n\nx = limits^max text for  limits^max - limits^min  varepsilon\n\nlimits^min leq x leq limits^max text otherwise \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_range_constraints!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_semicontinuous_ramp_constraints!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{S}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{<:ConstraintType}, Type{S}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Type{<:AbstractNetworkModel}}} where {S<:Union{ActivePowerVariable, PowerAboveMinimumVariable}, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"add_semicontinuous_ramp_constraints!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    T::Type{<:ConstraintType},\n    U::Type{S<:Union{ActivePowerVariable, PowerAboveMinimumVariable}},\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    _::Type{<:AbstractNetworkModel}\n)\n\n\nConstructs allowed rate-of-change constraints from variables, initial condtions, start/stop status, and rate data\n\nEquations\n\nIf t = 1:\n\nvariable[name, 1] - initial_conditions[ix].value <= rate_data[1][ix].up + rate_data[2][ix].max*varstart[name, 1]\n\ninitial_conditions[ix].value - variable[name, 1] <= rate_data[1][ix].down + rate_data[2][ix].min*varstop[name, 1]\n\nIf t > 1:\n\nvariable[name, t] - variable[name, t-1] <= rate_data[1][ix].up + rate_data[2][ix].max*varstart[name, t]\n\nvariable[name, t-1] - variable[name, t] <= rate_data[1][ix].down + rate_data[2][ix].min*varstop[name, t]\n\nLaTeX\n\nr^down + r^min x^stop_1 leq x_1 - x_init leq r^up + r^max x^start_1 text for  t = 1\n\nr^down + r^min x^stop_t leq x_t - x_t-1 leq r^up + r^max x^start_t forall t geq 2\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_semicontinuous_ramp_constraints!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_semicontinuous_range_constraints!-Union{Tuple{X}, Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Type{X}}} where {T<:ConstraintType, U<:VariableType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, X<:AbstractNetworkModel}","page":"Public API","text":"add_semicontinuous_range_constraints!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{U<:VariableType},\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    _::Type{X<:AbstractNetworkModel}\n)\n\n\nConstructs min/max range constraint from device variable and on/off decision variable.\n\nIf device min = 0:\n\nvarcts[name, t] <= limits.max*varbin[name, t])\n\nvarcts[name, t] >= 0.0\n\nOtherwise:\n\nvarcts[name, t] <= limits.max*varbin[name, t]\n\nvarcts[name, t] >= limits.min*varbin[name, t]\n\nwhere limits in constraint_infos.\n\nLaTeX\n\n0 leq x^cts leq limits^max x^bin text for  limits^min = 0\n\nlimits^min x^bin leq x^cts leq limits^max x^bin text otherwise \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_semicontinuous_range_constraints!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_service_variables!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, U, V, Type{F}}} where {D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, T<:VariableType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D}, Vector{D}}, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"add_service_variables!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    service::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    contributing_devices::Union{Array{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    _::Type{F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nAdd variables to the OptimizationContainer for a single service and its contributing devices.\n\nAll services of a given (VariableType, ServiceType) share a single sparse container keyed by (service_name, device_name, time), rather than one dense container per service disambiguated by a meta = service_name field. The container is created lazily on the first service of a type, and each subsequent call appends that service's slice, so separate formulation groups sharing a service type append to the same container.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_service_variables!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_slacked_range_constraints!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Any, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Any, Any}} where {T<:ConstraintType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"add_slacked_range_constraints!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    array,\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    slack_ub,\n    slack_lb;\n    constraint_names\n)\n\n\nConstructs a min/max range constraint from a device variable with OPTIONAL slack variables.\n\nThis is the slack-aware sibling of add_range_constraints!. It emits the same lb <= var <= ub pair (keyed with the usual \"lb\"/\"ub\" meta), but when slack containers are supplied it relaxes the bounds:\n\nvar[name, t] - slack_ub[name, t] <= limits.max var[name, t] + slack_lb[name, t] >= limits.min\n\nThe slack is subtracted on the upper bound and added on the lower bound. Passing nothing for either slack array recovers the plain bound for that direction.\n\nBecause the slack VARIABLE TYPES are owned downstream (e.g. POM), the caller passes the already-built JuMP slack containers (DenseAxisArrays) directly rather than a variable type. The array (the variable being constrained) and the devices to iterate are also passed in, so callers can route a subset of devices through this helper (e.g. only the static-rated branches, leaving a parameterized-RHS path elsewhere).\n\nArguments\n\narray: the JuMP container of the variable being bounded (e.g. FlowActivePowerVariable).\nslack_ub / slack_lb: JuMP slack containers, or nothing to omit slack in that direction.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_slacked_range_constraints!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_sparse_pwl_interpolation_variables!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Any, DeviceModelForBranches{U, V}}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Any, DeviceModelForBranches{U, V}, Any}} where {T<:Union{BinaryInterpolationVariableType, InterpolationVariableType}, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"add_sparse_pwl_interpolation_variables!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:Union{BinaryInterpolationVariableType, InterpolationVariableType}},\n    devices,\n    model::DeviceModel{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\nadd_sparse_pwl_interpolation_variables!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:Union{BinaryInterpolationVariableType, InterpolationVariableType}},\n    devices,\n    model::DeviceModel{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    num_segments\n)\n\n\nadd_sparse_pwl_interpolation_variables!(container, devices, ::T, model, num_segments = DEFAULT_INTERPOLATION_LENGTH)\n\nAdd piecewise linear interpolation variables to an optimization container.\n\nThis function creates the necessary variables for piecewise linear (PWL) approximation in optimization models. It adds either continuous interpolation variables (δ) or binary interpolation variables (z) depending on the variable type T. These variables are used in the incremental method for PWL approximation where:\n\nInterpolation variables (δ): Continuous variables ∈ [0,1] that represent weights for each segment\nBinary interpolation variables (z): Binary variables that enforce ordering constraints in incremental method\n\nThe function creates a 3-dimensional variable structure indexed by (devicename, segmentindex, time_step). For binary variables, the number of variables is one less than for continuous variables since they control transitions between segments.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: The optimization container to add variables to\ndevices: Collection of devices for which to create PWL variables\n::T: Type parameter specifying the variable type (InterpolationVariableType or BinaryInterpolationVariableType)\nmodel::DeviceModel{U, V}: Device model containing formulation information for bounds\nnum_segments::Int: Number of linear segments in the PWL approximation (default: DEFAULTINTERPOLATIONLENGTH)\n\nType Parameters\n\nT <: Union{InterpolationVariableType, BinaryInterpolationVariableType}: Variable type to create\nU <: IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent: Component type for devices\nV <: AbstractDeviceFormulation: Device formulation type for bounds\n\nNotes\n\nBinary variables have num_segments - 1 variables (control transitions between segments)\nContinuous variables have num_segments variables (one per segment)\nVariable bounds are set based on the device formulation if available\nVariables are created for all devices and time steps in the optimization horizon\n\nSee Also\n\n_add_generic_incremental_interpolation_constraint!: Function that uses these variables in constraints\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_sparse_pwl_interpolation_variables!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_time_series_parameter_container!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Type{V}, String, Any, Any, Any, UnitRange{Int64}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.TimeSeriesParameter, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesData}","page":"Public API","text":"add_time_series_parameter_container!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.TimeSeriesParameter},\n    ::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    ::Type{V<:InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesData},\n    name::String,\n    param_axs,\n    multiplier_axs,\n    additional_axs,\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64};\n    sparse,\n    meta\n) -> ParameterContainer\n\n\nAllocate a time-series parameter container (TimeSeriesAttributes). Parameter and multiplier arrays may have different first axes, so this is the only builder using the split-axes allocator.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_time_series_parameter_container!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_to_expression!-Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{<:ExpressionType}, Type{<:VariableType}, Any, DeviceModel, NetworkModel}","page":"Public API","text":"add_to_expression!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    expression_type::Type{<:ExpressionType},\n    variable_type::Type{<:VariableType},\n    devices,\n    model::DeviceModel,\n    network_model::NetworkModel\n)\n\n\nadd_to_expression!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    expression_type::Type{<:ExpressionType},\n    variable_type::Type{<:VariableType},\n    devices,\n    model::DeviceModel,\n    network_model::NetworkModel,\n)\n\nAdd device variables to system-wide expression. This is a generic fallback that errors - specific implementations should override.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_to_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_value_parameter_container!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, V, Vararg{Any}}} where {T<:VariableValueParameter, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:OptimizationContainerKey}","page":"Public API","text":"add_variable_value_parameter_container!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:VariableValueParameter},\n    ::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    source_key::OptimizationContainerKey,\n    axs...;\n    sparse,\n    meta\n) -> Union{ParameterContainer{T, U, A} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray, A<:VariableValueAttributes}, ParameterContainer{T, U, A} where {T<:AbstractArray, U<:(JuMP.Containers.SparseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N), A<:VariableValueAttributes}}\n\n\nAllocate a parameter container fed by another container's values (VariableValueAttributes). source_key is the variable/aux-variable key supplying those values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_value_parameter_container!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variables!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, U, Type{F}}} where {D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, T<:VariableType, U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D}, Vector{D}}, F}","page":"Public API","text":"add_variables!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    devices::Union{Array{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    _::Type{F}\n)\n\n\nAdds a variable to the optimization model and to the affine expressions contained in the optimization_container model according to the specified sign. Based on the inputs, the variable can be specified as binary.\n\nBounds\n\nlb_value_function <= varstart[name, t] <= ub_value_function\n\nIf binary = true:\n\nvarstart[name, t] in {0,1}\n\nLaTeX\n\nlb le x^device_t le ub forall t\n\nx^device_t in 01 forall t iff textbinary = true\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\ndevices : Vector or Iterator with the devices\nvar_key::VariableKey : Base Name for the variable\nbinary::Bool : Select if the variable is binary\nexpressionname::Symbol : Expressionname name stored in container.expressions to add the variable\nsign::Float64 : sign of the addition of the variable to the expression_name. Default Value is 1.0\n\nAccepted Keyword Arguments\n\nubvalue : Provides the function over device to obtain the value for a upperbound\nlbvalue : Provides the function over device to obtain the value for a lowerbound. If the variable is meant to be positive define lb = x -> 0.0\ninitial_value : Provides the function over device to obtain the warm start value\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variables!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variables!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, U, Any}} where {D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, T<:AuxVariableType, U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D}, Vector{D}}}","page":"Public API","text":"add_variables!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:AuxVariableType},\n    devices::Union{Array{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    formulation\n)\n\n\nDefault implementation of adding auxiliary variable to the model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variables!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_compact_retrospective!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}}, Matrix{InitialCondition}, Type{C}, Type{T}}} where {C<:ConstraintType, T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"device_duration_compact_retrospective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    duration_data::Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}},\n    initial_duration::Matrix{InitialCondition},\n    _::Type{C<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}\n)\n\n\nThis formulation of the duration constraints adds over the start times looking backwards.\n\nLaTeX\n\nMinimum up-time constraint:\n\nsum_i=t-min(d_min^up T)+ 1^t x_i^start - x_t^on leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nMinimum down-time constraint:\n\nsum_i=t-min(d_min^down T) + 1^t x_i^stop + x_t^on leq 1\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nduration_data::Vector{UpDown} : gives how many time steps variable needs to be up or down\ninitial_duration::Matrix{InitialCondition} : gives initial conditions for up (column 1) and down (column 2)\ncons_name::Symbol : name of the constraint\nvar_keys::Tuple{VariableKey, VariableKey, VariableKey}) : names of the variables\n: var_keys[1] : varon\n: var_keys[2] : varstart\n: var_keys[3] : varstop\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_compact_retrospective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_parameters!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}}, Matrix{InitialCondition}, Type{C}, Type{T}}} where {C<:ConstraintType, T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"device_duration_parameters!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    duration_data::Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}},\n    initial_duration::Matrix{InitialCondition},\n    _::Type{C<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}\n)\n\n\nThis formulation of the duration constraints considers parameters.\n\nLaTeX\n\nMinimum up-time constraint:\n\nIf t leq d_min^up\n\nd_min^downx_t^stop - sum_i=t-d_min^up + 1^t x_i^on - x_init^up leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps. Otherwise:\n\nsum_i=t-d_min^up + 1^t x_i^start - x_t^on leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nMinimum down-time constraint:\n\nIf t leq d_min^down\n\nd_min^upx_t^start - sum_i=t-d_min^down + 1^t (1 - x_i^on) - x_init^down leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps. Otherwise:\n\nsum_i=t-d_min^down + 1^t x_i^stop + x_t^on leq 1\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nduration_data::Vector{UpDown} : gives how many time steps variable needs to be up or down\ninitialdurationon::Vector{InitialCondition} : gives initial number of time steps variable is up\ninitialdurationoff::Vector{InitialCondition} : gives initial number of time steps variable is down\ncons_name::Symbol : name of the constraint\nvar_keys::Tuple{VariableKey, VariableKey, VariableKey}) : names of the variables\n: var_keys[1] : varon\n: var_keys[2] : varstart\n: var_keys[3] : varstop\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_parameters!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_retrospective!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}}, Matrix{InitialCondition}, Type{C}, Type{T}}} where {C<:ConstraintType, T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"device_duration_retrospective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    duration_data::Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}},\n    initial_duration::Matrix{InitialCondition},\n    _::Type{C<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}\n)\n\n\nThis formulation of the duration constraints adds over the start times looking backwards.\n\nLaTeX\n\nMinimum up-time constraint:\n\nIf t leq d_min^up - d_init^up and d_init^up  0\n\n1 + sum_i=t-d_min^up + 1^t x_i^start - x_t^on leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps. Otherwise:\n\nsum_i=t-d_min^up + 1^t x_i^start - x_t^on leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nMinimum down-time constraint:\n\nIf t leq d_min^down - d_init^down and d_init^down  0\n\n1 + sum_i=t-d_min^down + 1^t x_i^stop + x_t^on leq 1\n\nfor i in the set of time steps. Otherwise:\n\nsum_i=t-d_min^down + 1^t x_i^stop + x_t^on leq 1\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nduration_data::Vector{UpDown} : gives how many time steps variable needs to be up or down\ninitial_duration::Matrix{InitialCondition} : gives initial conditions for up (column 1) and down (column 2)\ncons_name::Symbol : name of the constraint\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_retrospective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.evaluate!-Tuple{AbstractEvaluationData, Any, Any}","page":"Public API","text":"evaluate!(data::AbstractEvaluationData, container, system)\n\n\nRun the evaluation: read state from container/system, write aux-variable inputs back into container, and mark data as solved. Concrete methods are registered in downstream packages.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.evaluate!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.export_outputs-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs}","page":"Public API","text":"export_outputs(\n    outputs::OptimizationProblemOutputs;\n    kwargs...\n)\n\n\nExports all outputs from the operations problem.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.export_outputs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.fill_slacked_range_constraints!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Any, Any, Type{T}, Any, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V}, Vector{V}}, DeviceModelForBranches{V, W}, Any, Any}} where {T<:ConstraintType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"fill_slacked_range_constraints!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    con_ub,\n    con_lb,\n    _::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    array,\n    devices::Union{Array{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    _::DeviceModel{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    slack_ub,\n    slack_lb\n)\n\n\nFill pre-created upper/lower bound constraint containers with slack-aware range constraints for devices. Use this (rather than add_slacked_range_constraints!) when the constraint containers must span a wider axis than devices — e.g. when another code path fills the remaining entries of the same (T, V) containers (such as a parameterized-RHS rating path). See add_slacked_range_constraints! for the slack convention.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.fill_slacked_range_constraints!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_all_constraint_index-Tuple{AbstractOptimizationModel}","page":"Public API","text":"get_all_constraint_index(\n    model::AbstractOptimizationModel\n) -> Vector{Tuple{ConstraintKey, Int64, Int64}}\n\n\nEach Tuple corresponds to (conname, internalindex, moi_index)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_all_constraint_index"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_all_variable_index-Tuple{AbstractOptimizationModel}","page":"Public API","text":"get_all_variable_index(\n    model::AbstractOptimizationModel\n) -> Vector{T} where T<:Tuple{Any, Int64, Int64}\n\n\nEach Tuple corresponds to (conname, internalindex, moi_index)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_all_variable_index"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_contingency_matrix","page":"Public API","text":"The contingency matrix derived during instantiation. Implemented downstream.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_contingency_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_incompatible_devices-Tuple{Dict}","page":"Public API","text":"get_incompatible_devices(\n    devices_template::Dict\n) -> Set{DataType}\n\n\nReturn the set of device types whose formulation is FixedOutput (incompatible with service provision).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_incompatible_devices"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_inner_data-Tuple{AbstractEvaluationData}","page":"Public API","text":"get_inner_data(data::AbstractEvaluationData)\n\n\nReturn the underlying domain-specific data wrapped by data (e.g., a PowerFlowData for a power-flow evaluator). Used by aux-variable calculators that need direct read access to the evaluator's output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_inner_data"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_min_max_limits-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, Type{T}, Type{F}}} where {T<:ConstraintType, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"get_min_max_limits(\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    _::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Get minimum and maximum limits for a given component, constraint type, and device formulation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_min_max_limits"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_network_matrix","page":"Public API","text":"The network matrix derived during instantiation. Implemented in the matrix-aware downstream package, which owns the concrete AbstractNetworkData.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_network_matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_network_reduction","page":"Public API","text":"The network reduction derived during instantiation. Implemented downstream.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_network_reduction"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_proportional_cost_per_system_unit-Tuple{Float64, InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem, Float64, Float64}","page":"Public API","text":"get_proportional_cost_per_system_unit(\n    cost_term::Float64,\n    unit_system::InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem,\n    system_base_power::Float64,\n    device_base_power::Float64\n) -> Any\n\n\nProportional (slope) cost coefficient normalized to system base.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_proportional_cost_per_system_unit"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_pwl_cost_expression_delta-Tuple{AbstractVector{JuMP.VariableRef}, AbstractVector{Float64}, Float64}","page":"Public API","text":"get_pwl_cost_expression_delta(\n    pwl_vars::AbstractVector{JuMP.VariableRef},\n    slopes::AbstractVector{Float64},\n    multiplier::Float64\n) -> JuMP.AffExpr\n\n\nCompute PWL objective expression from delta variables and slopes.\n\nReturns the objective expression without adding it to the objective (caller decides whether to use invariant or variant).\n\nobjective_term = Σ δ[i] * slope[i] * multiplier\n\nArguments\n\npwl_vars: vector of PWL delta variables\nslopes: vector of slope values (rate per segment, already normalized)\nmultiplier: additional multiplier (e.g., dt for time resolution)\n\nReturns\n\nJuMP affine expression representing the objective function term.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_pwl_cost_expression_delta"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_quadratic_cost_per_system_unit-Tuple{Float64, InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem, Float64, Float64}","page":"Public API","text":"get_quadratic_cost_per_system_unit(\n    cost_term::Float64,\n    unit_system::InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem,\n    system_base_power::Float64,\n    device_base_power::Float64\n) -> Any\n\n\nQuadratic cost coefficient normalized to system base.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_quadratic_cost_per_system_unit"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.initialize_evaluation_data-Tuple{AbstractEvaluator, Any, Any}","page":"Public API","text":"initialize_evaluation_data(\n    ev::AbstractEvaluator,\n    container,\n    system\n)\n\n\nBuild the runtime state for ev and return an AbstractEvaluationData. Called once during OptimizationContainer construction. Concrete methods are registered in downstream packages.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.initialize_evaluation_data"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_from_evaluator-Tuple{Type{<:AuxVariableType}}","page":"Public API","text":"is_from_evaluator(_::Type{<:AuxVariableType}) -> Bool\n\n\nExtension point: Check if an auxiliary variable type is produced by an external evaluator (see AbstractEvaluator). Default: false. Override in POM for evaluator-bound aux variable subtypes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_from_evaluator"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_solved-Tuple{AbstractEvaluationData}","page":"Public API","text":"is_solved(data::AbstractEvaluationData)\n\n\nReturn true if data has been solved in the current iteration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_solved"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_aux_variable-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Public API","text":"read_aux_variable(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    args...;\n    kwargs...\n) -> DataFrame\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested aux_variable key for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\naux_variable::Tuple{Type{<:AuxVariableType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent} : Tuple with aux_variable type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_aux_variable"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_aux_variables-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Outputs}","page":"Public API","text":"read_aux_variables(\n    res::InfrastructureSystems.Outputs;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Dict\n\n\nReturn the values for all auxiliary variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_aux_variables"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_aux_variables-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Any}","page":"Public API","text":"read_aux_variables(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    aux_variables;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Union{Dict{Any, Any}, Dict{_A, DataFrame} where _A}\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested aux_variable keys for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\naux_variables::Vector{Tuple{Type{<:AuxVariableType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}} : Tuple with aux_variable type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_aux_variables"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_dual-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Public API","text":"read_dual(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    args...;\n    kwargs...\n) -> DataFrame\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested dual key for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\ndual::Tuple{Type{<:ConstraintType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent} : Tuple with dual type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_dual"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_duals-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Outputs}","page":"Public API","text":"read_duals(\n    res::InfrastructureSystems.Outputs;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Dict\n\n\nReturn the values for all duals.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_duals"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_duals-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Any}","page":"Public API","text":"read_duals(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    duals;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Union{Dict{Any, Any}, Dict{_A, DataFrame} where _A}\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested dual keys for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\nduals::Vector{Tuple{Type{<:ConstraintType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}} : Tuple with dual type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_duals"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_expression-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Public API","text":"read_expression(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    args...;\n    kwargs...\n) -> DataFrame\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested expression key for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\nexpression::Tuple{Type{<:ExpressionType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent} : Tuple with expression type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_expression"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_expressions-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Outputs}","page":"Public API","text":"read_expressions(\n    res::InfrastructureSystems.Outputs;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Union{Dict{Any, Any}, Dict{_A, DataFrame} where _A}\n\n\nReturn the values for all expressions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_expressions"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_expressions-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs}","page":"Public API","text":"read_expressions(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Union{Dict{Any, Any}, Dict{_A, DataFrame} where _A}\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested expression keys for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\nexpressions::Vector{Tuple{Type{<:ExpressionType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}} : Tuple with expression type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_expressions"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_parameter-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Public API","text":"read_parameter(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    args...;\n    kwargs...\n) -> DataFrame\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested parameter key for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\nparameter::Tuple{Type{<:ParameterType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent} : Tuple with parameter type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_parameter"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_parameters-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Outputs}","page":"Public API","text":"read_parameters(\n    res::InfrastructureSystems.Outputs;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Dict\n\n\nReturn the values for all parameters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_parameters"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_parameters-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Any}","page":"Public API","text":"read_parameters(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    parameters;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Union{Dict{Any, Any}, Dict{_A, DataFrame} where _A}\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested parameter keys for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\nparameters::Vector{Tuple{Type{<:ParameterType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}} : Tuple with parameter type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_parameters"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_variable-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Vararg{Any}}","page":"Public API","text":"read_variable(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    args...;\n    kwargs...\n) -> DataFrame\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested variable key for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\nres::OptimizationProblemOutputs: Optimization problem outputs\nvariable::Tuple{Type{<:VariableType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}: Tuple with variable type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime: Start time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\ntable_format::TableFormat: Format of the table to be returned. Default is TableFormat.LONG where the columns are DateTime, name, and value when the data has two dimensions and DateTime, name, name2, and value when the data has three dimensions. Set to it TableFormat.WIDE to pivot the names as columns. Note: TableFormat.WIDE is not supported when the data has more than two dimensions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_variable"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_variables-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Outputs}","page":"Public API","text":"read_variables(\n    res::InfrastructureSystems.Outputs;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Dict\n\n\nReturn the values for all variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_variables"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_variables-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, Any}","page":"Public API","text":"read_variables(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    variables;\n    kwargs...\n) -> Union{Dict{Any, Any}, Dict{_A, DataFrame} where _A}\n\n\nReturn the values for the requested variable keys for a problem. Accepts a vector of keys for the return of the values.\n\nArguments\n\nvariables::Vector{Tuple{Type{<:VariableType}, Type{<:IS.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}} : Tuple with variable type and device type for the desired outputs\nstart_time::Dates.DateTime : initial time of the requested outputs\nlen::Int: length of outputs\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_variables"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.requires_initialization-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"requires_initialization(\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation\n) -> Bool\n\n\nrequires_initialization(formulation::AbstractDeviceFormulation)\n\nCheck if a device formulation requires initial conditions. Default implementation returns false. Override for formulations with state variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.requires_initialization"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.reset!-Tuple{AbstractEvaluationData}","page":"Public API","text":"reset!(data::AbstractEvaluationData)\n\n\nMark data as not-yet-solved for the current iteration. Called by calculate_aux_variables! at the top of each pass.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.reset!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.serialize_optimization_model-Tuple{OptimizationContainer, String}","page":"Public API","text":"serialize_optimization_model(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    save_path::String\n)\n\n\nExports the OpModel JuMP object in MathOptFormat\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.serialize_optimization_model"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.serialize_outputs-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, AbstractString}","page":"Public API","text":"serialize_outputs(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    directory::AbstractString\n)\n\n\nSerialize the outputs to a binary file.\n\nIt is recommended that directory be the directory that contains a serialized AbstractOptimizationModel. That will allow automatic deserialization of the PowerSystems.System. The OptimizationProblemOutputs instance can be deserialized with OptimizationProblemOutputs(directory).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.serialize_outputs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_event_model!-Union{Tuple{B}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{DeviceModelForBranches{D, B}, AbstractEventKey, AbstractEventModel}} where {D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, B<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Public API","text":"set_event_model!(\n    model::DeviceModel{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, B<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    key::AbstractEventKey,\n    event_model::AbstractEventModel\n)\n\n\nset_event_model!(model::DeviceModel, key::AbstractEventKey, event_model::AbstractEventModel)\n\nAttach an event (contingency) model to model under key. Errors if key is already present.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_event_model!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_ic_quantity!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{InitialCondition{T, Float64}, Float64}} where T<:InitialConditionType","page":"Public API","text":"set_ic_quantity!(\n    ic::InitialCondition{T<:InitialConditionType, Float64},\n    var_value::Float64\n)\n\n\nDefault implementation of setinitialcondition_value\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_ic_quantity!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_ic_quantity!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{InitialCondition{T, JuMP.VariableRef}, Float64}} where T<:InitialConditionType","page":"Public API","text":"set_ic_quantity!(\n    ic::InitialCondition{T<:InitialConditionType, JuMP.VariableRef},\n    var_value::Float64\n)\n\n\nDefault implementation of setinitialcondition_value\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_ic_quantity!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_source_data!-Tuple{OptimizationProblemOutputs, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsType}","page":"Public API","text":"set_source_data!(\n    res::OptimizationProblemOutputs,\n    source::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsType\n)\n\n\nSet the system in the outputs instance.\n\nDoes not verify that source produced these outputs: the only identity IOM records is source_data_uuid, and resolving it for a domain system is the caller's job. Callers that can check should do so before calling (see PowerAnalytics' load_outputs).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_source_data!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.supports_outages-Tuple{Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}}","page":"Public API","text":"supports_outages(\n    _::Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n) -> Bool\n\n\nsupports_outages(::Type{<:AbstractDeviceFormulation}) -> Bool\n\nTrait declaring whether a device formulation consumes DeviceModel.outages. Defaults to false. POM specializes this to true for security-constrained branch formulations (AbstractSecurityConstrainedStaticBranch).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.supports_outages"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.update_container_parameter_values!","page":"Public API","text":"update_container_parameter_values!(optimization_container, model, key, input)\n\nUpdate parameter values in the optimization container from the given input data. This is an extension point — concrete implementations should be defined in PowerOperationsModels (or PowerSimulations for simulation-specific variants).\n\nOnly called in emulation_model.jl: that file's contents and this function should likely be moved to POM or PSI.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.update_container_parameter_values!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.update_initial_conditions!-Tuple{Vector{<:InitialCondition}, EmulationModelStore{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InMemoryDataset}, Dates.Millisecond}","page":"Public API","text":"update_initial_conditions!(\n    ics::Vector{<:InitialCondition},\n    store::EmulationModelStore{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InMemoryDataset},\n    resolution::Dates.Millisecond\n)\n\n\nupdate_initial_conditions!(ics, store, resolution)\n\nUpdate initial conditions from the emulation model store. This is an extension point - concrete implementations for specific initial condition types should be defined in PowerOperationsModels.\n\nArguments\n\nics: Vector of InitialCondition objects to update\nstore: EmulationModelStore containing the recorded values\nresolution: Time resolution (Dates.Millisecond)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.update_initial_conditions!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.update_initial_conditions!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractOptimizationModel, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InitialConditionKey{T, U}, Any}} where {T<:InitialConditionType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Public API","text":"update_initial_conditions!(\n    model::AbstractOptimizationModel,\n    key::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InitialConditionKey{T<:InitialConditionType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    source\n)\n\n\nupdate_initial_conditions!(model, key, source)\n\nUpdate initial conditions for a specific key from the model store. Dispatches to the per-IC-type update_initial_conditions!(ics, store, resolution) method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.update_initial_conditions!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.uses_commitment_variables-Tuple{Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}}","page":"Public API","text":"uses_commitment_variables(\n    _::Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}\n) -> Bool\n\n\nTrait function: does device type T use commitment (on/off) variables? Defaults to false; POM specializes for thermal device types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.uses_commitment_variables"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/public/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.variable_cost-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter, Type{<:VariableType}, Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}, Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}}","page":"Public API","text":"variable_cost(\n    cost::InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter,\n    _::Type{<:VariableType},\n    _::Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    _::Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: variable cost.\n\nThe one exception where it isn't just get_variable(cost): storage devices, where we need to map ActivePower{In/Out} to {charge/discharge} variable cost.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.variable_cost"},{"category":"section","location":"how_to_guides/stub/","page":"-","text":"Please refer to the How-to-Guides section of the diataxis framework.","title":"-"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Quadratic-Approximations","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"This module provides three methods for approximating x^2 as a piecewise linear (PWL) function within a MIP framework. Each method produces a JuMP AffExpr that can be used in constraints or objectives wherever x^2 would appear.\n\nAll three methods share a common interface: they accept a vector of component names, a range of time steps, a container of x variables, domain bounds, an approximation resolution parameter, and a meta string that identifies the variable type being approximated. The meta parameter allows creating multiple independent approximations for the same component type (e.g., one for active power and another for reactive power).","title":"Quadratic Approximations"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Solver-SOS2","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Approximates x^2 using a convex combination of breakpoints with solver-native SOS2 constraints for adjacency enforcement.","title":"Solver SOS2"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Formulation","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Given N uniformly spaced breakpoints x_1 ldots x_N on x_min x_max:\n\nVariables:\n\nlambda_i in 0 1 quad i = 1 ldots N\n\nConstraints:\n\nbeginaligned\nx = sum_i=1^N lambda_i  x_i  text(linking) \nsum_i=1^N lambda_i = 1  text(normalization) \nlambda in textSOS2  text(adjacency solver-native)\nendaligned\n\nApproximation:\n\nhatx^2 = sum_i=1^N lambda_i  x_i^2","title":"Formulation"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Complexity","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"For S segments (N = S + 1 breakpoints): N continuous variables, N + 1 constraints, plus one SOS2 set per component per time step. The approximation error decreases as O(1S^2).","title":"Complexity"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Variables-and-Constraints","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Container Type Description\nQuadraticVariable Lambda (lambda) convex combination weights\nSOS2LinkingConstraint Links x to weighted breakpoints\nSOS2NormConstraint Ensures sum lambda_i = 1","title":"Variables and Constraints"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Manual-SOS2","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Identical approximation to Solver SOS2, but replaces the solver-native SOS2 constraint with explicit binary variables and linear inequality constraints. This is useful for solvers that do not support SOS2 constraints natively.","title":"Manual SOS2"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Additional-Formulation","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"In addition to the linking and normalization constraints above, manual SOS2 introduces N - 1 binary segment-selection variables z_j in 0 1 and enforces adjacency via:\n\nbeginaligned\nsum_j=1^N-1 z_j = 1  text(exactly one active segment) \nlambda_1 leq z_1 \nlambda_i leq z_i-1 + z_i  i = 2 ldots N-1 \nlambda_N leq z_N-1\nendaligned","title":"Additional Formulation"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Complexity-2","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"For S segments: N continuous variables + S binary variables, N + S + 2 linear constraints per component per time step. Same approximation quality as Solver SOS2.","title":"Complexity"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Variables-and-Constraints-2","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Container Type Description\nQuadraticVariable Lambda (lambda) convex combination weights\nManualSOS2BinaryVariable Binary segment-selection variables (z)\nSOS2LinkingConstraint Links x to weighted breakpoints\nSOS2NormConstraint Ensures sum lambda_i = 1\nManualSOS2SegmentSelectionConstraint Ensures sum z_j = 1","title":"Variables and Constraints"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Sawtooth","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Approximates x^2 using the recursive sawtooth MIP formulation from Beach, Burlacu, Hager, and Hildebrand (2023). This method requires only O(log(1varepsilon)) binary variables to achieve error varepsilon, compared to O(1sqrtvarepsilon) for the SOS2 methods.","title":"Sawtooth"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Formulation-2","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Given depth L and Delta = x_max - x_min:\n\nVariables:\n\nbeginaligned\ng_j in 0 1 quad j = 0 ldots L  text(auxiliary continuous) \nalpha_j in 0 1 quad j = 1 ldots L  text(binary)\nendaligned\n\nConstraints:\n\nbeginaligned\ng_0 = fracx - x_minDelta  text(linking) \ng_j leq 2 g_j-1  j = 1 ldots L \ng_j leq 2(1 - g_j-1)  j = 1 ldots L \ng_j geq 2(g_j-1 - alpha_j)  j = 1 ldots L \ng_j geq 2(alpha_j - g_j-1)  j = 1 ldots L\nendaligned\n\nApproximation:\n\nhatx^2 = x_min^2 + (2 x_min Delta + Delta^2) g_0 - sum_j=1^L Delta^2 cdot 2^-2j g_j","title":"Formulation"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Complexity-3","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"For depth L: L + 1 continuous variables + L binary variables, 4L + 1 constraints per component per time step. The approximation interpolates x^2 at 2^L + 1 uniformly spaced breakpoints with maximum overestimation error Delta^2 cdot 2^-2L-2.","title":"Complexity"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Variables-and-Constraints-3","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Container Type Description\nSawtoothAuxVariable Auxiliary continuous variables (g_0 ldots g_L)\nSawtoothBinaryVariable Binary variables (alpha_1 ldots alpha_L)\nSawtoothLinkingConstraint Links g_0 to normalized x","title":"Variables and Constraints"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Comparison","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Property Solver SOS2 Manual SOS2 Sawtooth\nBinary variables 0 S L\nContinuous variables S + 1 S + 1 L + 1\nBreakpoints S + 1 S + 1 2^L + 1\nMax error O(Delta^2  S^2) O(Delta^2  S^2) Delta^2 cdot 2^-2L-2\nSolver requirements SOS2 support MIP only MIP only\n\nTo match the number of breakpoints between methods, set S = 2^L. At equal breakpoint count the approximation quality is identical, but the sawtooth uses L = log_2 S binary variables instead of S.","title":"Comparison"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Error-Scaling","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Both SOS2 and sawtooth produce the same PWL interpolation of x^2 when they use the same number of uniform breakpoints. With n uniform segments on 0 1, the interpolant F_n(x) satisfies the classical error bound (Barmann et al., 2023):\n\n0 leq F_n(x) - x^2 leq frac14n^2 quad textfor all  x in 0 1\n\nThe maximum error is attained at the midpoint of each segment. Since both methods interpolate at the same breakpoints, the pointwise error is identical — the difference lies entirely in how efficiently the segments are encoded.","title":"Error Scaling"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Same-number-of-binary-variables","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"If we budget L binary/integer variables for each method, SOS2 gets L segments while sawtooth gets 2^L segments. The error gap grows exponentially:\n\nL SOS2 segments SOS2 error Sawtooth segments Sawtooth error Ratio\n1 1 250times10^-1 2 625times10^-2 4x\n2 2 625times10^-2 4 156times10^-2 4x\n3 3 278times10^-2 8 391times10^-3 7x\n4 4 156times10^-2 16 977times10^-4 16x\n5 5 100times10^-2 32 244times10^-4 41x\n6 6 694times10^-3 64 610times10^-5 114x\n7 7 510times10^-3 128 153times10^-5 334x\n8 8 391times10^-3 256 381times10^-6 1024x\n\nSOS2 error decays polynomially as O(1L^2); sawtooth error decays exponentially as O(4^-L).","title":"Same number of binary variables"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Same-number-of-segments","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"When both methods use the same number of uniform segments n, they produce identical PWL interpolations, so the approximation error is the same. The difference is in formulation size: SOS2 needs O(n) binary variables, sawtooth needs only log_2(n).\n\nSegments n Error SOS2 vars Sawtooth vars Var ratio\n2 625times10^-2 1 1 1.0x\n4 156times10^-2 3 2 1.5x\n8 391times10^-3 7 3 2.3x\n16 977times10^-4 15 4 3.8x\n32 244times10^-4 31 5 6.2x\n64 610times10^-5 63 6 10.5x\n128 153times10^-5 127 7 18.1x\n256 381times10^-6 255 8 31.9x","title":"Same number of segments"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Extension-to-Bilinear-Terms","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Bilinear terms z = xy arise throughout optimization (energy systems, pooling problems, gas networks). The standard univariate reformulation uses the identity:\n\nxy = frac14left(x + y)^2 - (x - y)^2right\n\nEach squared term is approximated independently with one of the methods above. With both terms at the same refinement level, the bilinear error satisfies:\n\nvarepsilon_xy leq frac12  varepsilon_textquad\n\nAll scaling relationships from the univariate case carry over with a constant factor of 12. The exponential gap between SOS2 and sawtooth persists.","title":"Extension to Bilinear Terms"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#Practical-Considerations","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"SOS2 has the advantage of being natively supported by commercial solvers (Gurobi, CPLEX) with specialized branching rules. Both the solver SOS2 and manual SOS2 formulations produce sharp LP relaxations for convex functions.\n\nSawtooth introduces auxiliary continuous variables and big-M-type constraints, which may interact less favorably with presolve and cutting planes. However, Beach et al. (2023) show that the sawtooth relaxation is sharp (its LP relaxation equals the convex hull) and hereditarily sharp (sharpness is preserved at every node in the branch-and-bound tree). This strong theoretical property, combined with exponentially fewer binary variables, can lead to significant solver performance gains for problems requiring high approximation accuracy.\n\nWhether the tighter approximation at a given variable budget outweighs the structural advantages of SOS2 depends on the specific problem and solver.","title":"Practical Considerations"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/quadratic_approximations/#References","page":"Quadratic Approximations","text":"Beach, B., Burlacu, R., Barmann, A., Hager, L., Kleinert, T. (2023). Enhancements of discretization approaches for non-convex MIQCQPs. Journal of Global Optimization.\nBarmann, A., Burlacu, R., Hager, L., Kleinert, T. (2023). On piecewise linear approximations of bilinear terms: structural comparison of univariate and bivariate MIP formulations. Journal of Global Optimization, 85, 789-819.\nYarotsky, D. (2017). Error bounds for approximations with deep ReLU networks. Neural Networks, 94, 103-114.\nHuchette, J.A. (2018). Advanced mixed-integer programming formulations: methodology, computation, and application. PhD thesis, MIT.","title":"References"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Piecewise-Linear-Cost-Functions","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"","title":"Piecewise Linear Cost Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#What-Is-a-Piecewise-Linear-Cost-Function?","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"In power systems, the cost to produce electricity from a generator is rarely a straight line. As you push a generator harder, the marginal cost of each additional MW often changes. A piecewise linear (PWL) cost function approximates this curve by connecting a series of straight-line segments between breakpoints.\n\nFor example, a generator might have the following cost structure:\n\nPower Output (MW) Marginal Cost ($/MWh)\n50 (min) 20\n100 25\n150 35\n200 (max) 50\n\nThis means the first 50 MW above minimum costs $20/MWh, the next 50 MW costs $25/MWh, and so on. The total cost is the sum of the cost of each segment.\n\nThis package provides two formulations for encoding such curves into a JuMP optimization model. Both express an operating point and its cost as a point on a piecewise linear curve connecting breakpoints (P_0 C_0) (P_1 C_1) ldots (P_n C_n), but they approach the problem differently.","title":"What Is a Piecewise Linear Cost Function?"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#How-IOM-and-POM-Work-Together","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels (IOM) provides the mathematical formulations — the variables, constraints, and expressions that encode a PWL curve into JuMP. It does not decide which cost type applies to which device.\n\nPowerOperationsModels (POM) provides the device-specific routing — it knows that a ThermalGen with MarketBidCost should use the delta formulation, or that a RenewableDispatch with CostCurve{PiecewisePointCurve} should use the lambda formulation.\n\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph PSY [\"PowerSystems (PSY)\"]\n        CC[\"CostCurve / FuelCurve\"]\n        MBC[\"MarketBidCost\"]\n        IEC[\"ImportExportCost\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph POM [\"PowerOperationsModels (POM)\"]\n        Route[\"Route cost type\\nto formulation\"]\n        Params[\"Populate parameters\\n(device-specific)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph IOM [\"InfrastructureOptimizationModels (IOM)\"]\n        Lambda[\"Lambda Formulation\\n(convex combination)\"]\n        Delta[\"Delta Formulation\\n(block offers)\"]\n        Obj[\"JuMP Objective\"]\n    end\n\n    CC --> Route\n    MBC --> Route\n    IEC --> Route\n    Route --> Lambda\n    Route --> Delta\n    Route --> Params\n    Params --> Delta\n    Lambda --> Obj\n    Delta --> Obj\n\nIn short:\n\nPOM decides which formulation to use for each device and cost type.\nIOM builds the JuMP variables, constraints, and objective expressions.\nCost data comes from PSY (PowerSystems.jl) components.","title":"How IOM and POM Work Together"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Lambda-Formulation-(Convex-Combination)","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Used by CostCurve{PiecewisePointCurve} and FuelCurve{PiecewisePointCurve}.\n\nThe lambda formulation assigns a weight lambda_i to each breakpoint. The operating point and cost are expressed as a weighted average of the breakpoint values. Think of it as saying: \"The generator is operating at a mix of these known cost points.\"","title":"Lambda Formulation (Convex Combination)"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Visual-Intuition","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"graph TD\n    subgraph \"Lambda Formulation\"\n        direction TB\n        A[\"Breakpoints: (P₀,C₀), (P₁,C₁), ..., (Pₙ,Cₙ)\"]\n        B[\"Weights: λ₀, λ₁, ..., λₙ\"]\n        C[\"Power: p = Σ λᵢ Pᵢ\"]\n        D[\"Cost: C(p) = Σ λᵢ C(Pᵢ)\"]\n        E[\"Constraint: Σ λᵢ = 1\"]\n        A --> B\n        B --> C\n        B --> D\n        B --> E\n    end","title":"Visual Intuition"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Formulation","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Given n + 1 breakpoints with power levels P_0 ldots P_n and costs C(P_0) ldots C(P_n):\n\nVariables:\n\nlambda_i in 0 1 quad i = 0 1 ldots n\n\nConstraints:\n\nbeginaligned\np = sum_i=0^n lambda_i  P_i  text(linking) \nC(p) = sum_i=0^n lambda_i  C(P_i)  text(cost) \nsum_i=0^n lambda_i = u  text(normalization  u text = on-status) \ntextat most two adjacent  lambda_i text may be nonzero  text(adjacency)\nendaligned","title":"Formulation"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Adjacency-Enforcement","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"The adjacency condition keeps the operating point on a single line segment. For convex cost curves (where each segment is more expensive than the last), the optimizer naturally satisfies this condition — no extra constraints are needed.\n\nFor non-convex cost curves, an SOS2 constraint is added to enforce adjacency explicitly. This requires solver support for SOS2, and effectively introduces additional branching in the solver.","title":"Adjacency Enforcement"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Compact-Form","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"When the power variable represents output above minimum generation (PowerAboveMinimumVariable), a compact variant adjusts the linking constraint to include a P_min offset:\n\nsum_i=0^n lambda_i  P_i = p + P_min cdot u","title":"Compact Form"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Variables-and-Constraints","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Container Type Description\nPiecewiseLinearCostVariable Lambda weights lambda_i in 0 1\nPiecewiseLinearCostConstraint Links power variable to weighted breakpoints\nPiecewiseLinearCostNormalizationConstraint Ensures sum lambda_i = u","title":"Variables and Constraints"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Public-API","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Function Role\nadd_pwl_linking_constraint! Links power variable to weighted breakpoints\nadd_pwl_normalization_constraint! Ensures sum lambda_i = u\nadd_pwl_sos2_constraint! Adds SOS2 adjacency for non-convex curves\nadd_variable_cost_to_objective! Entry point — orchestrates variables, constraints, and cost","title":"Public API"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Delta-Formulation-(Incremental-/-Block-Offers)","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Used by MarketBidCost and ImportExportCost offer curves.\n\nThe delta formulation assigns a variable delta_k to each segment, representing how much of that segment has been used. Think of it as filling buckets: fill the cheapest bucket first, then the next cheapest, and so on.","title":"Delta Formulation (Incremental / Block Offers)"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Visual-Intuition-2","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"graph TD\n    subgraph \"Delta Formulation\"\n        direction TB\n        A[\"Segments with slopes: m₁, m₂, ..., mₙ\"]\n        B[\"Delta variables: δ₁, δ₂, ..., δₙ\"]\n        C[\"Power: p = Σ δₖ + Pmin\"]\n        D[\"Cost: C(p) = Σ mₖ × δₖ\"]\n        E[\"Capacity: δₖ ≤ Pₖ₊₁ - Pₖ\"]\n        A --> B\n        B --> C\n        B --> D\n        B --> E\n    end","title":"Visual Intuition"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Formulation-2","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Given n segments with breakpoints P_0 ldots P_n and marginal costs (slopes) m_k = fracC(P_k) - C(P_k-1)P_k - P_k-1:\n\nVariables:\n\ndelta_k geq 0 quad k = 1 ldots n\n\nConstraints:\n\nbeginaligned\np = sum_k=1^n delta_k + P_mintextoffset  text(linking) \ndelta_k leq P_k - P_k-1  text(segment capacity) \nC(p) = sum_k=1^n m_k  delta_k  text(cost)\nendaligned","title":"Formulation"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Convexity-Advantage","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"For convex offer curves (m_1 leq m_2 leq cdots leq m_n), the fill-order condition is automatically satisfied. A cost-minimizing optimizer fills cheap segments before expensive ones, so no SOS2 constraints or binary variables are needed. This is the common case in power systems, where generator marginal costs are typically increasing.","title":"Convexity Advantage"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Direction:-Incremental-vs-Decremental","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"The delta formulation supports two directions:\n\nIncremental (supply): Represents power produced. The generator fills segments from low to high cost. Uses PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOffer variables.\nDecremental (demand): Represents power consumed. The load fills segments from high to low willingness-to-pay. Uses PiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOffer variables.\n\nPOM determines which direction to use based on the device type and formulation.","title":"Direction: Incremental vs Decremental"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Variables-and-Constraints-2","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Container Type Description\nPiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOffer Delta variables for incremental offers\nPiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOffer Delta variables for decremental offers\nPiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOfferConstraint Linking + capacity for incremental\nPiecewiseLinearBlockDecrementalOfferConstraint Linking + capacity for decremental","title":"Variables and Constraints"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Public-API-2","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Function Role\nadd_pwl_variables! Creates n delta variables per time step\nadd_pwl_term! Orchestrates variables, constraints, and cost expression\nget_pwl_cost_expression Builds sum m_k  delta_k cost expression\nadd_pwl_block_offer_constraints! Low-level block-offer constraint builder\nadd_variable_cost_to_objective! Entry point for offer curve costs","title":"Public API"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Comparison","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":" Lambda (lambda) Delta (delta)\nThinks about Breakpoints (the dots) Segments (the lines)\nVariables n + 1 (one per breakpoint) n (one per segment)\nOutput equation p = sum lambda_i  P_i p = sum delta_k + P_min\nCost equation C = sum lambda_i  C(P_i) C = sum m_k  delta_k\nAdjacency rule Must be enforced explicitly (SOS2) Often automatic (convex case)\nBinary variables Usually needed (non-convex) Often not needed (convex case)\nUsed by CostCurve, FuelCurve MarketBidCost, ImportExportCost","title":"Comparison"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#When-Does-the-Choice-Matter?","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"For convex cost functions — where each segment costs more than the last — the delta formulation is typically simpler and faster. The optimizer fills cheap segments first on its own, so no extra adjacency constraints are needed. This is the common case in power systems.\n\nFor non-convex cost functions — where a segment might be cheaper than the one before it — both formulations need additional constraints (SOS2 or binary variables) to force the correct ordering. In that case the lambda formulation is the traditional choice.","title":"When Does the Choice Matter?"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Cost-Type-Routing","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"The following table summarizes which cost data types route to which PWL formulation:\n\nCost Data Type Formulation Notes\nCostCurve{PiecewisePointCurve} Lambda Direct (x, y) breakpoints\nFuelCurve{PiecewisePointCurve} Lambda Fuel consumption curve x fuel price\nCostCurve{PiecewiseIncrementalCurve} Lambda (converted) Converted to PiecewisePointCurve first\nCostCurve{PiecewiseAverageCurve} Lambda (converted) Converted to PiecewisePointCurve first\nMarketBidCost (offer curves) Delta Slopes + breakpoints; supports time-varying\nImportExportCost (offer curves) Delta Import/export block offers\nCostCurve{TimeSeriesPiecewiseIncrementalCurve} Delta Time-series-backed; always time-varying\n\nflowchart TD\n    CostType{\"What type of\\ncost data?\"}\n\n    CostType -->|\"PiecewisePointCurve\\n(breakpoints with costs)\"| Lambda[\"Lambda Formulation\"]\n    CostType -->|\"PiecewiseIncrementalCurve\\n(slopes)\"| Convert[\"Convert to\\nPiecewisePointCurve\"]\n    CostType -->|\"MarketBidCost /\\nImportExportCost\"| Delta[\"Delta Formulation\"]\n    CostType -->|\"TimeSeriesPiecewise-\\nIncrementalCurve\"| DeltaTS[\"Delta Formulation\\n(time-varying)\"]\n\n    Convert --> Lambda\n\n    Lambda --> InvObj[\"Invariant Objective\\n(computed once)\"]\n    Delta -->|\"Static curves\"| InvObj\n    Delta -->|\"Time-varying curves\"| VarObj[\"Variant Objective\\n(rebuilt each step)\"]\n    DeltaTS --> VarObj","title":"Cost Type Routing"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#The-IOM-POM-Boundary","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"The following diagram shows where IOM's responsibility ends and POM's begins:\n\nflowchart TB\n    subgraph POM [\"POM (PowerOperationsModels)\"]\n        A1[\"Detect cost type on device\"]\n        A2[\"Validate cost data\"]\n        A3[\"Populate parameter containers\\n(slopes, breakpoints per time step)\"]\n        A4[\"Implement proportional_cost\\nfor each device type\"]\n        A5[\"Override objective_function_multiplier\\n(e.g., -1 for loads)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph IOM [\"IOM (InfrastructureOptimizationModels)\"]\n        B1[\"Create PWL variables\\n(lambda or delta)\"]\n        B2[\"Add linking and capacity\\nconstraints\"]\n        B3[\"Build cost expressions\"]\n        B4[\"Route to invariant or\\nvariant objective\"]\n        B5[\"process_market_bid_parameters!\\n(orchestration)\"]\n    end\n\n    A1 --> B5\n    A2 --> B5\n    B5 --> A3\n    A3 --> B1\n    B1 --> B2\n    B2 --> B3\n    A4 --> B3\n    A5 --> B3\n    B3 --> B4\n\nIOM provides:\n\nMathematical formulations (lambda, delta)\nPWL variable and constraint creation\nObjective expression building\nParameter orchestration (process_market_bid_parameters!, process_import_export_parameters!)\n\nPOM provides:\n\nDevice-specific cost routing (add_variable_cost_to_objective! overloads)\nParameter population (add_parameters! implementations)\nCost term extraction (proportional_cost implementations)\nObjective sign/multiplier overrides","title":"The IOM-POM Boundary"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Incremental-Interpolation-(General-PWL-Approximation)","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"In addition to cost functions, the package provides a general-purpose incremental (delta) method for approximating arbitrary nonlinear functions as piecewise linear. This is used for PWL approximation of constraints (e.g., loss functions, quadratic terms).","title":"Incremental Interpolation (General PWL Approximation)"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Formulation-3","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Given breakpoints (x_1 y_1) ldots (x_n+1 y_n+1) where y_i = f(x_i), and interpolation variables delta_i in 0 1 with binary ordering variables z_i in 0 1:\n\nbeginaligned\nx = x_1 + sum_i=1^n delta_i  (x_i+1 - x_i) \ny = y_1 + sum_i=1^n delta_i  (y_i+1 - y_i) \nz_i geq delta_i+1 quad z_i leq delta_i quad text(ordering)\nendaligned\n\nThe ordering constraints ensure segments are filled sequentially: delta_1 must be filled before delta_2 can begin.","title":"Formulation"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/piecewise_linear_objective_functions/#Public-API-3","page":"Piecewise Linear Objective Functions","text":"Function Role\nadd_sparse_pwl_interpolation_variables! Creates delta and z variables","title":"Public API"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Time-Varying-Objective-Functions","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"","title":"Time-Varying Objective Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Overview","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"In power systems optimization, costs can be either static (constant for the entire simulation) or time-varying (changing at each time step). For example:\n\nA gas generator might have a static heat rate curve that never changes.\nAn electricity market might have time-varying offer prices that change every hour based on market conditions.\n\nIOM supports both cases. The key difference is how the objective function terms are stored and updated:\n\nProperty Static (Invariant) Time-Varying (Variant)\nCost data source Directly from the component From parameter containers\nObjective storage Invariant expression Variant expression\nWhen computed Once at model build time Rebuilt at each simulation step\nTypical use CostCurve, FuelCurve MarketBidCost with time series\n\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Static [\"Static Path\"]\n        S1[\"Cost data on\\ncomponent\"] --> S2[\"Build JuMP\\nexpression once\"]\n        S2 --> S3[\"Invariant\\nObjective\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph TimeVarying [\"Time-Varying Path\"]\n        T1[\"Time series\\ndata\"] --> T2[\"Store in\\nparameter containers\"]\n        T2 --> T3[\"Read parameters\\nat each time step\"]\n        T3 --> T4[\"Variant\\nObjective\"]\n    end\n\n    S3 --> Obj[\"Total Objective\\n= Invariant + Variant\"]\n    T4 --> Obj","title":"Overview"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#How-Parameters-Enable-Time-Varying-Costs","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"When a cost is time-varying, the raw cost data (e.g., slopes and breakpoints of an offer curve) changes at each time step. IOM stores this data in parameter containers — typed arrays indexed by [device, time] or [device, segment, time].","title":"How Parameters Enable Time-Varying Costs"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#The-Parameter-Decomposition-Pipeline","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"Consider a generator with a MarketBidCost whose offer curves come from a time series. The data flows through three stages:\n\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Stage1 [\"Stage 1: Storage (PSY)\"]\n        TS[\"Time series of\\nPiecewiseStepData objects\"]\n        TSK[\"TimeSeriesKey stored\\non MarketBidCost field\"]\n        TS --- TSK\n    end\n\n    subgraph Stage2 [\"Stage 2: Decomposition (IOM + POM)\"]\n        Slopes[\"Slope parameters\\n[device, segment, time]\"]\n        BPs[\"Breakpoint parameters\\n[device, point, time]\"]\n        CostMin[\"Cost-at-min parameters\\n[device, time]\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Stage3 [\"Stage 3: Objective Construction (IOM)\"]\n        DeltaVars[\"Delta variables\\nδ₁, δ₂, ..., δₙ\"]\n        Constraints[\"Linking + capacity\\nconstraints\"]\n        CostExpr[\"Cost expression\\nΣ mₖ × δₖ × dt\"]\n        VarObj[\"Variant objective\"]\n    end\n\n    TSK -->|\"process_market_bid_parameters!\"| Slopes\n    TSK -->|\"process_market_bid_parameters!\"| BPs\n    TSK -->|\"process_market_bid_parameters!\"| CostMin\n    Slopes --> CostExpr\n    BPs --> Constraints\n    DeltaVars --> Constraints\n    DeltaVars --> CostExpr\n    CostExpr --> VarObj\n\nStage 1 — Storage: PSY stores each cost field independently. An offer curve is stored as a time series of PiecewiseStepData objects, each containing slopes and breakpoints for one time step.\n\nStage 2 — Decomposition: IOM's process_market_bid_parameters! orchestrates the decomposition. For each parameter type, it checks which devices have time series data, validates the data, and delegates to POM's add_parameters! to populate the containers. POM splits each PiecewiseStepData into separate slope and breakpoint arrays for JuMP.\n\nStage 3 — Objective Construction: At each time step, IOM reads the slopes and breakpoints from the parameter containers and builds the delta PWL objective terms. Because the data changes per step, the cost expression is added to the variant objective.","title":"The Parameter Decomposition Pipeline"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Parameter-Types","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"IOM defines the following parameter types for time-varying offer curve costs:","title":"Parameter Types"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Piecewise-Linear-Parameters","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"These store the decomposed PWL data from offer curves:\n\nParameter Type Stores Array Axes Used For\nIncrementalPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter Marginal rates (slopes) [device, segment, t] PWL cost expression\nIncrementalPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter Power levels (breakpoints) [device, point, t] PWL linking constraints\nDecrementalPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter Marginal rates (decremental) [device, segment, t] Decremental PWL cost expression\nDecrementalPiecewiseLinearBreakpointParameter Power levels (decremental) [device, point, t] Decremental PWL constraints","title":"Piecewise Linear Parameters"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Scalar-Cost-Parameters","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"These store single-valued costs that may vary over time:\n\nParameter Type Stores Array Axes Used For\nIncrementalCostAtMinParameter Cost at minimum power [device, t] On-variable proportional cost\nDecrementalCostAtMinParameter Cost at min (decremental) [device, t] Decremental on-variable cost\nStartupCostParameter Start-up cost [device, t] Start-up cost term\nShutdownCostParameter Shut-down cost [device, t] Shut-down cost term\nFuelCostParameter Fuel price [device, t] Fuel curve cost multiplier","title":"Scalar Cost Parameters"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#How-Parameters-Are-Read","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"At each time step t, the objective function reads from parameter containers. Each parameter container has two arrays:\n\nparameter_array: The raw value (e.g., slope in $/MWh).\nmultiplier_array: A scaling factor (e.g., for unit conversion).\n\nThe effective value is: parameter_array[name, t] * multiplier_array[name, t].","title":"How Parameters Are Read"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Invariant-vs-Variant-Objective","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"The optimization container maintains two separate objective expressions:\n\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Build [\"Model Build Time\"]\n        StaticCosts[\"Static costs\\n(CostCurve, FuelCurve)\"]\n        TVCosts[\"Time-varying costs\\n(MarketBidCost with time series)\"]\n        StaticCosts --> InvExpr[\"Invariant Expression\\n(fixed for all steps)\"]\n        TVCosts --> VarExpr[\"Variant Expression\\n(rebuilt each step)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Solve [\"Each Simulation Step\"]\n        Update[\"Update parameter\\nvalues from new data\"]\n        Rebuild[\"Rebuild variant\\nexpression\"]\n        Combine[\"Total Objective =\\nInvariant + Variant\"]\n        Update --> Rebuild\n        InvExpr --> Combine\n        Rebuild --> Combine\n    end\n\nInvariant expression: Computed once during model construction. Contains cost terms whose coefficients never change (e.g., a generator with a fixed heat rate curve). These terms are added via add_cost_term_invariant! or add_to_objective_invariant_expression!.\n\nVariant expression: Rebuilt at each simulation step when parameter values are updated. Contains cost terms whose coefficients come from time-varying parameters. These terms are added via add_cost_term_variant! or add_to_objective_variant_expression!.\n\nWhy the split? In rolling-horizon simulations (e.g., EmulationModel), the model is solved repeatedly with updated data. Invariant terms do not need to be recomputed, saving time. Only variant terms are cleared and rebuilt with fresh parameter values.","title":"Invariant vs Variant Objective"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Time-Varying-PWL:-End-to-End-Example","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"Consider a thermal generator \"gen1\" with a MarketBidCost whose incremental offer curves come from a time series. Here is the full flow:","title":"Time-Varying PWL: End-to-End Example"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Step-1:-Parameter-Orchestration","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"IOM's process_market_bid_parameters! is called during model construction:\n\nFilters devices that have MarketBidCost.\nFor each parameter type (slopes, breakpoints, cost-at-min, startup, shutdown):\nValidates the cost data on each device.\nChecks which devices have time series for that parameter.\nCalls POM's add_parameters! to create and populate the parameter container.\n\nflowchart TD\n    PMB[\"process_market_bid_parameters!\"]\n    PMB --> SU[\"StartupCostParameter\"]\n    PMB --> SD[\"ShutdownCostParameter\"]\n    PMB --> CAM[\"IncrementalCostAtMinParameter\"]\n    PMB --> Slopes[\"IncrementalPiecewiseLinear-\\nSlopeParameter\"]\n    PMB --> BPs[\"IncrementalPiecewiseLinear-\\nBreakpointParameter\"]\n\n    SU --> Validate[\"Validate + filter\\ndevices with time series\"]\n    SD --> Validate\n    CAM --> Validate\n    Slopes --> Validate\n    BPs --> Validate\n\n    Validate --> AddP[\"POM: add_parameters!\\n(populate containers)\"]","title":"Step 1: Parameter Orchestration"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Step-2:-Objective-Function-Construction","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"For each time step, add_pwl_term! reads from the parameter containers:\n\nRead data: Fetches slopes and breakpoints from parameter arrays for device \"gen1\" at time t.\nCreate variables: Creates delta variables delta_1 delta_2 ldots delta_n via add_pwl_variables!.\nAdd constraints: Adds linking constraint p = sum delta_k + P_mintextoffset and segment capacity constraints delta_k leq P_k+1 - P_k.\nBuild cost: Computes C = sum m_k cdot delta_k cdot Delta t via get_pwl_cost_expression.\nAdd to variant objective: Since the slopes come from parameters, the cost expression is added to the variant objective.","title":"Step 2: Objective Function Construction"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Step-3:-Simulation-Updates","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"In a rolling-horizon simulation:\n\nNew time series data arrives (e.g., updated market prices).\nParameter containers are updated with fresh slope and breakpoint values.\nThe variant objective expression is cleared and rebuilt.\nThe model is re-solved with the updated objective.","title":"Step 3: Simulation Updates"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#Time-Varying-Proportional-Costs","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"Not all time-varying costs are piecewise linear. Some are simple proportional (linear) costs that change over time. For example:\n\nFuel cost: A FuelCurve with a time-varying fuel price.\nOn-variable cost: The cost at minimum generation from a MarketBidCost.\nStart-up / shut-down costs: May vary by time step.\n\nThese use the scalar parameter types (FuelCostParameter, IncrementalCostAtMinParameter, StartupCostParameter, ShutdownCostParameter) and follow the same variant/invariant pattern:\n\nflowchart LR\n    Check{\"Is cost\\ntime-varying?\"}\n    Check -->|\"No\"| Static[\"add_cost_term_invariant!\\n(rate is a constant)\"]\n    Check -->|\"Yes\"| TV[\"add_cost_term_variant!\\n(rate from parameter)\"]\n    Static --> InvObj[\"Invariant Objective\"]\n    TV --> VarObj[\"Variant Objective\"]\n\nFor start-up and shut-down costs, the functions add_start_up_cost! and add_shut_down_cost! handle the static/time-varying branching automatically.\n\nFor proportional costs (e.g., on-variable cost for thermal generators), add_proportional_cost_maybe_time_variant! queries POM's proportional_cost implementation at each time step and routes the result to the appropriate objective expression.","title":"Time-Varying Proportional Costs"},{"category":"section","location":"explanation/time_varying_objective_functions/#The-IOM-POM-Extension-Pattern-for-Parameters","page":"Time-Varying Objective Functions","text":"The parameter system follows an extension pattern where IOM orchestrates and POM implements:\n\nResponsibility IOM POM\nDefine parameter types IncrementalPiecewiseLinearSlopeParameter, etc. —\nOrchestrate parameter creation process_market_bid_parameters! —\nValidate device-specific constraints Generic validation Device-specific overloads (e.g., multi-start units)\nPopulate parameter containers — add_parameters! implementations\nRead parameters during objective build add_pwl_term!, add_cost_term_variant! —\nDetermine if cost is time-varying — is_time_variant_proportional implementations\nExtract proportional cost per step — proportional_cost implementations\n\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant POM as POM\n    participant IOM as IOM\n    participant JuMP as JuMP Model\n\n    Note over POM,JuMP: Model Construction\n    POM->>IOM: process_market_bid_parameters!(container, devices, model)\n    IOM->>IOM: Validate cost data\n    IOM->>IOM: Filter devices with time series\n    IOM->>POM: add_parameters!(container, SlopeParam, devices, model)\n    POM->>IOM: Populate slope parameter container\n    IOM->>POM: add_parameters!(container, BreakpointParam, devices, model)\n    POM->>IOM: Populate breakpoint parameter container\n\n    Note over POM,JuMP: Objective Construction\n    POM->>IOM: add_variable_cost_to_objective!(container, var, component, cost, form)\n    IOM->>IOM: add_pwl_term! for each time step\n    IOM->>IOM: Read slopes/breakpoints from parameters\n    IOM->>JuMP: Create delta variables\n    IOM->>JuMP: Add constraints\n    IOM->>JuMP: Add cost to variant objective\n\n    Note over POM,JuMP: Simulation Step Update\n    POM->>IOM: Update parameter values\n    IOM->>JuMP: Rebuild variant objective\n\nThis separation allows IOM to remain agnostic about specific device types while POM provides the domain knowledge needed to populate parameters and route costs correctly.","title":"The IOM-POM Extension Pattern for Parameters"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/developer_guidelines/#Developer-Guidelines","page":"Developer Guidelines","text":"In order to contribute to InfrastructureOptimizationModels.jl repository please read the following sections of InfrastructureSystems.jl documentation in detail:\n\nStyle Guide\nContributing Guidelines\n\nPull requests are always welcome to fix bugs or add additional modeling capabilities.\n\nAll the code contributions need to include tests with a minimum coverage of 70%","title":"Developer Guidelines"},{"category":"section","location":"#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.jl","page":"Welcome Page","text":"","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Overview","page":"Welcome Page","text":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.jl is a Julia package that provides core abstractions and optimization model structures for power systems operations modeling. It defines DecisionModel and EmulationModel types along with their associated optimization containers, formulations, and output handling capabilities.","title":"Overview"},{"category":"section","location":"#About","page":"Welcome Page","text":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels is part of the National Lab of the Rockies NLR (formerly known as NREL) Sienna ecosystem, an open source framework for scheduling problems and dynamic simulations for power systems. The Sienna ecosystem can be found on github. It contains three applications:\n\nSienna\\Data enables efficient data input, analysis, and transformation\nSienna\\Ops enables enables system scheduling simulations by formulating and solving optimization problems\nSienna\\Dyn enables system transient analysis including small signal stability and full system dynamic simulations\n\nEach application uses multiple packages in the Julia programming language.","title":"About"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/internal/#Internal-API","page":"Internals","text":"","title":"Internal API"},{"category":"constant","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IGNORABLE_FILES","page":"Internals","text":"If the name of an extraneous file that appears in simulation outputs matches one of these regexes, it is safe to ignore\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.IGNORABLE_FILES"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearApproxConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Abstract supertype for bilinear approximation method configurations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearApproxConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearProductExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for bilinear product (x·y) approximation results.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearProductExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearProductLinkingConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Constraint container for linking product expressions and variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearProductLinkingConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearProductVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Variable container for bilinear product (x ̇y) approximation results.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.BilinearProductVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config","page":"Internals","text":"Config for Bin2 bilinear approximation using z = ½((x+y)² − x² − y²).\n\nFields\n\nquad_config::Q: quadratic method used for x², y², and (x+y)²\nadd_mccormick::Bool: whether to add reformulated McCormick cuts through separable variables (default true)\n\nThe Q type parameter lets tolerance helpers dispatch on the inner quad method; see tolerance_depth(::Type{Bin2Config{Q}}; …).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for double-NMDT bilinear approximation (discretizes both x and y).\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: number of binary discretization levels L for both x and y\n\nThe worst-case relaxation gap is Δx·Δy·2^{-2L-2}. See tolerance_depth(::Type{DNMDTBilinearConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for double-NMDT quadratic approximation.\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: number of binary discretization levels L\nepigraph_depth::Int: depth of an additional epigraph Q^{L1} lower bound; 0 disables (default 3×depth)\n\nThe DNMDT side gives worst-case |result_expr − x²| ≤ Δ²·2^{-2L-2} (two-sided magnitude bound). The binary discretization x = x_grid + δ is exact in MIP (binary×binary and binary×continuous McCormick are tight at integer β), but the residual δ² term is approximated by a McCormick envelope on (δ, δ) over [0, 2^{-L}]² — and continuous×continuous McCormick has slack at interior δ even at integer β. So result_expr floats in an interval around x² whose half-width is at most Δ²·2^{-2L-2} (max gap at δ = 2^{-L-1}).\n\nWhen epigraph_depth = L_e > 0, the McCormick lower bounds on the binary–continuous products are dropped and a lower bound result_expr ≥ epigraph(x) is added in their place. The result remains two-sided around x², but the lower envelope is now the global epigraph instead of the per-product McCormick LBs; worst case becomes max(Δ²·2^{-2L-2}, Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4}). Contrast with pwmcc_segments on the SOS2 variants, which adds genuine LP cuts and never changes the MIP-feasible set.\n\nSee tolerance_depth(::Type{DNMDTQuadConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance, and tolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{DNMDTQuadConfig}; …) for the matching epigraph_depth.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModelStore","page":"Internals","text":"Stores outputs data for one DecisionModel\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DecisionModelStore"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for epigraph quadratic approximation results.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphQuadConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for epigraph (Q^{L1}) LP-only lower-bound quadratic approximation.\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: sawtooth recursion depth L; pure LP, zero binary variables\n\nThe worst-case underestimation gap is Δ²·2^{-2L-4} — the sawtooth-epigraph relaxation bound from Beach, Burlacu, Hager, Hildebrand 2024 (Definition 6, Proposition 2). The construction adds tangent cuts z ≥ fʲ(x, g) − 2^{-2j-2} for j = 0, 1, …, L plus the two boundary tangents to x² at x = xmin and x = xmax. The j = 0 cut is the tangent to x² at the segment midpoint; without it, the gap degrades to Δ²·2^{-2L-2}. See tolerance_depth(::Type{EpigraphQuadConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphQuadConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphTangentConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Tangent-line lower-bound constraints in epigraph relaxation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphTangentConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphTangentExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Tangent-line lower-bound expression fL used in the epigraph formulation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphTangentExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Variable representing a lower-bounded approximation of x² in epigraph relaxation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ExportParameters","page":"Internals","text":"Typed container for export configuration parameters used during model output writing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ExportParameters"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSBoundConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Two-sided HybS bound constraints: Bin2 lower + Bin3 upper.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSBoundConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for HybS (Hybrid Separable) bilinear approximation.\n\nAdds two inequalities that sandwich z ≈ x·y:\n\nlower: z ≥ ½(z_p1 − z_x − z_y) where z_p1 ≤ (x+y)² is an epigraph (LP-only) lower bound and z_x ≥ x², z_y ≥ y² come from the inner quadratic Q.\nupper: z ≤ ½(z_x + z_y − z_p2) where z_p2 ≤ (x−y)² is an epigraph (LP-only) lower bound on the cross-difference.\n\nFields\n\nquad_config::Q: quadratic method for the shared x² and y² terms\nepigraph_depth::Int: depth for the epigraph approximation of cross-terms (x±y)²\nadd_mccormick::Bool: whether to add standard McCormick envelope cuts on the product variable (default false)\n\nQ must be a strictly one-sided-over quadratic approximation (so z_x ≥ x² and z_y ≥ y² hold at every MIP-feasible point). With a two-sided or one-sided-under inner Q the sandwich can become infeasible. Sketch: let ε_Q ≥ 0 bound |z_• − •²| and ε_E ≥ 0 bound (•)² − z_p•. With zx, zy two-sided (each can be ≤ x² by up to εQ) and zp1, z_p2 at their lowest:\n\nLower − Upper = ½(z_p1 + z_p2) − z_x − z_y\n              = ½((x+y)² − ε_E + (x−y)² − ε_E) − (x² − ε_Q) − (y² − ε_Q)\n              = x² + y² − ε_E − x² − y² + 2ε_Q\n              = 2ε_Q − ε_E\n\nSo Lower > Upper whenever 2ε_Q > ε_E — model infeasible. This rules out EpigraphQuadConfig (one-sided under, so z_x has no MIP-feasible upper bound) and NMDTQuadConfig / DNMDTQuadConfig (two-sided in both regimes: at epigraph_depth = 0 the McCormick on the δ·δ or δ·xh residual product has slack even at integer β, and at epigraph_depth > 0 the result floats in [epigraph(x), nmdt(x)]). Only SawtoothQuadConfig, SolverSOS2QuadConfig, and ManualSOS2QuadConfig are supported. See tolerance_depth(::Type{HybSConfig{Q}}; …) and tolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{HybSConfig{Q}}; …).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2AdjacencyConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Links active segment to lambda variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2AdjacencyConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2BinaryVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Binary segment-selection variables (z) for manual SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2BinaryVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for manual binary-variable SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: number of PWL segments (breakpoints = depth + 1)\npwmcc_segments::Int: number of piecewise McCormick cut partitions; 0 to disable (default 0)\n\nThe worst-case PWL overestimation gap is Δ²/(4·depth²). pwmcc_segments is an LP-relaxation tightener (adds piecewise-McCormick cuts on the concave relaxation surface); it does not change the MIP-optimal worst-case error, only the LP relaxation given to branch-and-bound.\n\nConstraint: pwmcc_segments must evenly divide depth (enforced by the constructor). The PWMCC chord upper bound is valid for the PWL value q only when every PWMCC boundary coincides with a PWL breakpoint, which on a uniform grid holds iff pwmcc_segments divides depth; otherwise a chord straddling a breakpoint cuts off MIP-feasible solutions (e.g. depth=3, pwmcc_segments=2 makes v ∈ (4/9, 5/9) infeasible). See tolerance_depth(::Type{ManualSOS2QuadConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2SegmentSelectionConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Ensures exactly one segment is active (∑zⱼ = 1) in manual SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2SegmentSelectionConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2SegmentSelectionExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression for the segment selection sum Σ z_j in manual SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2SegmentSelectionExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.McCormickConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Standard McCormick envelope constraints bounding the bilinear product z = x·y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.McCormickConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ModelInternal","page":"Internals","text":"Common structure to keep track of optimization models' internal information.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ModelInternal"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for single-NMDT bilinear approximation (discretizes x only).\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: number of binary discretization levels L for x\n\nThe worst-case relaxation gap is Δx·Δy·2^{-L-2}. See tolerance_depth(::Type{NMDTBilinearConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryContinuousProductConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"McCormick envelope constraints for binary-continuous products ui ≈ βi·y in NMDT.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryContinuousProductConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryContinuousProductExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for the NMDT binary-continuous product: Σ 2^{−i}·u_i ≈ β·y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryContinuousProductExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryContinuousProductVariable","page":"Internals","text":"McCormick linearization variables ui ≈ βi · y in NMDT binary-continuous products.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryContinuousProductVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Binary discretization variables β_i ∈ {0,1} in the NMDT decomposition of xh.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBinaryVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization","page":"Internals","text":"Stores the result of discretizing a normalized variable for use in NMDT products.\n\nFields:\n\nnorm_expr: affine expression for xh = (x − xmin)/(xmax − x_min) ∈ [0,1]\nbeta_var: binary variables β_i ∈ {0,1} indexed by (name, i, t)\ndelta_var: residual variables δ ∈ [0, 2^{−depth}] indexed by (name, t)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretizationExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for the NMDT binary discretization: Σ 2^{−i}·β_i + δ ≈ xh.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretizationExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTEDiscretizationConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Constraint enforcing xh = Σ 2^{−i}·β_i + δ in the NMDT discretization.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTEDiscretizationConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for single-NMDT quadratic approximation.\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: number of binary discretization levels L\nepigraph_depth::Int: depth of an additional epigraph Q^{L1} lower bound; 0 disables (default 3×depth)\n\nThe NMDT side gives worst-case |result_expr − x²| ≤ Δ²·2^{-L-2} two-sided magnitude bound (note the single L, not 2L — single NMDT discretizes only one factor). The binary discretization x = x_grid + δ is exact in MIP, but the cross term δ·xh (where xh is the full normalized x) is approximated by McCormick on (δ, xh) — both continuous — and that has slack at interior values even at integer β. So result_expr floats in a two-sided interval around x².\n\nWhen epigraph_depth = L_e > 0, the McCormick lower bounds on the binary–continuous products are dropped and a lower bound result_expr ≥ epigraph(x) is added in their place. The result remains two-sided around x², but the lower envelope is now the global epigraph instead of the per-product McCormick LBs; worst case becomes max(Δ²·2^{-L-2}, Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4}). Contrast with pwmcc_segments on the SOS2 variants, which adds genuine LP cuts and never changes the MIP-feasible set.\n\nSee tolerance_depth(::Type{NMDTQuadConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance, and tolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{NMDTQuadConfig}; …) for the matching epigraph_depth.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTResidualProductVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Variable z ≈ δ · y linearizing the residual-continuous product in NMDT.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTResidualProductVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTResidualVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Residual variable δ ∈ [0, 2^{−L}] capturing the NMDT discretization error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTResidualVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTResultExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for the final NMDT quadratic approximation result.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTResultExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTTightenConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Epigraph lower-bound tightening constraint on the NMDT quadratic result.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTTightenConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoBilinearApproxConfig","page":"Internals","text":"No-op bilinear config: returns exact x·y as a QuadExpr.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoBilinearApproxConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoQuadApproxConfig","page":"Internals","text":"No-op config: returns exact x² as a QuadExpr (for NLP-capable solvers or testing).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoQuadApproxConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NormedVariableExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for the normalized variable xh = (x − xmin) / (xmax − x_min) ∈ [0,1].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NormedVariableExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearCostConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Struct to create the PiecewiseLinearCostConstraint associated with a specified variable.\n\nSee the piecewise linear cost functions section for more information.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearCostConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearCostNormalizationConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Normalization constraint for PWL cost: sum of delta variables equals on-status.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseLinearCostNormalizationConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickBinary","page":"Internals","text":"Binary interval selector for piecewise McCormick cuts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickBinary"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickChordUB","page":"Internals","text":"Piecewise McCormick chord upper-bound constraint on v^2 approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickChordUB"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickDisaggregated","page":"Internals","text":"Disaggregated variable for piecewise McCormick cuts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickDisaggregated"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickIntervalLB","page":"Internals","text":"Interval activation lower bound: t{k-1} * deltak <= v^d_k.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickIntervalLB"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickIntervalUB","page":"Internals","text":"Interval activation upper bound: v^dk <= tk * delta_k.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickIntervalUB"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickLinking","page":"Internals","text":"Disaggregation linking constraint: v = sumk v^dk.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickLinking"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickSelectorSum","page":"Internals","text":"Selector sum constraint: sumk deltak = 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickSelectorSum"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickTangentLBL","page":"Internals","text":"Piecewise McCormick tangent lower-bound constraint (left endpoint).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickTangentLBL"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickTangentLBR","page":"Internals","text":"Piecewise McCormick tangent lower-bound constraint (right endpoint).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.PiecewiseMcCormickTangentLBR"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.QuadraticApproxConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Abstract supertype for quadratic approximation method configurations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.QuadraticApproxConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.QuadraticExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for quadratic (x²) approximation results.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.QuadraticExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.QuadraticVariable","page":"Internals","text":"lambda_var (λ) convex combination weight variables for SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.QuadraticVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ReformulatedMcCormickConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Reformulated McCormick constraints on Bin2 separable variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ReformulatedMcCormickConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2LinkingConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Links x to the weighted sum of breakpoints in SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2LinkingConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2LinkingExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression for the weighted sum of breakpoints Σ λi * xi linking x to lambda variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2LinkingExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2NormConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Ensures the sum of λ weights equals 1 in SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2NormConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2NormExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression for the normalization sum Σ λ_i in SOS2 quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SOS2NormExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothAuxVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Auxiliary continuous variables (g₀, …, g_L) for sawtooth quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothAuxVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothBinaryVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Binary variables (α₁, …, α_L) for sawtooth quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothBinaryVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothLPConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"LP relaxation constraints (gj ≤ 2g{j-1}, gj ≤ 2(1−g{j-1})) used in epigraph tightening.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothLPConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothLinkingConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Links g₀ to the normalized x value in sawtooth quadratic approximation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothLinkingConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothMIPConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Constrains gj based on g{j-1}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothMIPConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for sawtooth MIP quadratic approximation.\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: recursion depth L; uses L binary variables for 2^L + 1 breakpoints\nepigraph_depth::Int: depth of an additional epigraph Q^{L1} lower bound (0 disables, default 0)\n\nEffect of epigraph_depth on the worst-case error\n\nepigraph_depth = 0: the formulation is purely deterministic — result_expr = sawtooth(x) is pinned by the binary structure, so |z − x²| ≤ Δ²·2^{-2L-2} where Δ = max − min.\n\nepigraph_depth = L_e > 0: a free continuous variable z is introduced with z ≤ sawtooth(x) and z ≥ epigraph(x), and result_expr = z. This is a structural change, not just LP-tightening: the MIP-feasible set of result_expr values grows from a single point to the interval [epigraph(x), sawtooth(x)]. The worst-case error over that interval is\n\n|z − x²| ≤ max(Δ²·2^{-2L-2}, Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4})\n\nL_e ≥ L − 1: sawtooth dominates, worst-case = Δ²·2^{-2L-2}.\nL_e < L − 1: epigraph dominates, worst-case = Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4}.\n\nContrast with pwmcc_segments on the SOS2 variants, which adds genuine LP cuts and never changes the MIP-feasible set.\n\nSee tolerance_depth(::Type{SawtoothQuadConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance, and tolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{SawtoothQuadConfig}; …) for the matching epigraph_depth.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothTightenedConstraint","page":"Internals","text":"Bounds tightened variable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothTightenedConstraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothTightenedVariable","page":"Internals","text":"Variable result in tightened version.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothTightenedVariable"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2Constraint","page":"Internals","text":"Solver-native MOI.SOS2 adjacency constraint on lambda variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2Constraint"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig","page":"Internals","text":"Config for solver-native SOS2 quadratic approximation (MOI.SOS2 adjacency).\n\nFields\n\ndepth::Int: number of PWL segments (breakpoints = depth + 1)\npwmcc_segments::Int: number of piecewise McCormick cut partitions; 0 to disable (default 0)\n\nThe worst-case PWL overestimation gap is Δ²/(4·depth²). pwmcc_segments is an LP-relaxation tightener (adds piecewise-McCormick cuts on the concave relaxation surface); it does not change the MIP-optimal worst-case error, only the LP relaxation given to branch-and-bound.\n\nConstraint: pwmcc_segments must evenly divide depth (enforced by the constructor). The PWMCC chord upper bound is valid for the PWL value q only when every PWMCC boundary coincides with a PWL breakpoint, which on a uniform grid holds iff pwmcc_segments divides depth; otherwise a chord straddling a breakpoint cuts off MIP-feasible solutions (e.g. depth=3, pwmcc_segments=2 makes v ∈ (4/9, 5/9) infeasible). See tolerance_depth(::Type{SolverSOS2QuadConfig}; …) to derive depth from a target tolerance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.VariableDifferenceExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for subtracting variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.VariableDifferenceExpression"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.VariableSumExpression","page":"Internals","text":"Expression container for adding variables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.VariableSumExpression"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#Base.empty!-Tuple{EmulationModelStore}","page":"Internals","text":"empty!(store::EmulationModelStore)\n\n\nBase.empty!(store::EmulationModelStore)\n\nEmpty the EmulationModelStore\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.empty!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    xsq,\n    ysq,\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::Bin2Config, container, C, names, time_steps, xsq, ysq, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nPrecomputed form: Bin2 identity z = ½((x+y)² − x² − y²) with optional PWMCC concave cuts. Accepts pre-computed quadratic approximations xsq ≈ x² and ysq ≈ y².\n\nArguments\n\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::Bin2Config, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nStandard form: compute x² and y² quadratic approximations, then delegate to precomputed form.\n\nArguments\n\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::DNMDTBilinearConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x·y using the DNMDT method from raw variable inputs.\n\nDiscretizes both x and y independently via _discretize! then delegates to the pre-discretized overload.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::DNMDTBilinearConfig: configuration for the DNMDT bilinear approximation\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of x variables indexed by (name, t)\ny_var: container of y variables indexed by (name, t)\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    y_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::DNMDTBilinearConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_disc, y_disc, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x·y using the DNMDT method from pre-built discretizations.\n\nConstructs all four cross binary-continuous products (βx·yh, βy·δx, βy·xh, βx·δy) then delegates to the core DNMDT assembler. Stores results in a BilinearProductExpression container.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::DNMDTBilinearConfig: configuration for the DNMDT bilinear approximation\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_disc::NMDTDiscretization: pre-built discretization for x\ny_disc::NMDTDiscretization: pre-built discretization for y\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    xsq,\n    ysq,\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::HybSConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, xsq, ysq, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nHybS bilinear approximation with pre-computed quadratic approximations for x² and y².\n\nCombines Bin2 and Bin3 separable identities:\n\nBin2 lower bound: z ≥ ½(zp1 − zx − zy) where zp1 lower-bounds (x+y)²\nBin3 upper bound: z ≤ ½(zx + zy − zp2) where zp2 lower-bounds (x−y)²\n\nThe cross-terms (x+y)² and (x−y)² always use epigraph Q^{L1} (pure LP).\n\nArguments\n\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::HybSConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x·y using HybS (Hybrid Separable) relaxation with config-selected quadratic method.\n\nArguments\n\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::NMDTBilinearConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x·y using the NMDT method from raw variable inputs.\n\nDiscretizes x via _discretize! and normalizes y via _normed_variable!, then delegates to the pre-discretized overload.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::NMDTBilinearConfig: configuration for the NMDT bilinear approximation\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of x variables indexed by (name, t)\ny_var: container of y variables indexed by (name, t)\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    yh_expr,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(config::NMDTBilinearConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_disc, yh_expr, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x·y using the NMDT method from a pre-built x discretization and normalized y.\n\nDiscretizes only x (using x_disc) while y is already normalized to yh ∈ [0,1]. Computes binary-continuous product βx·yh and residual product δx·yh, then assembles x·y via _assemble_product!. Stores results in a BilinearProductExpression container.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::NMDTBilinearConfig: configuration for the NMDT bilinear approximation\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_disc::NMDTDiscretization: pre-built discretization for x\nyh_expr: expression container for the normalized variable yh = (y − ymin)/(ymax − y_min)\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoBilinearApproxConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    _::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoBilinearApproxConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    xsq,\n    ysq,\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(::NoBilinearApproxConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, xsq, ysq, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nPrecomputed-form no-op bilinear approximation: returns exact x·y as a QuadExpr. xsq and ysq are accepted for signature parity with the precomputed-form dispatches of Bin2Config and HybSConfig (so a caller can swap configs without changing the call site) but are unused here.\n\nArguments\n\n::NoBilinearApproxConfig: no-op configuration (no fields)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nxsq: precomputed x² container (ignored)\nysq: precomputed y² container (ignored)\nx_var: container of x variables indexed by (name, t)\ny_var: container of y variables indexed by (name, t)\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-component bounds on x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-component bounds on y\nmeta::String: variable type identifier for the approximation\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoBilinearApproxConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_bilinear_approx!(\n    _::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoBilinearApproxConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_bilinear_approx!(::NoBilinearApproxConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nNo-op bilinear approximation: returns exact x·y as a QuadExpr.\n\nArguments\n\n::NoBilinearApproxConfig: no-op configuration (no fields)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of x variables indexed by (name, t)\ny_var: container of y variables indexed by (name, t)\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y domain\nmeta::String: variable type identifier for the approximation\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_bilinear_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_container!-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{E}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Type{E}, Bool, Vararg{Any, N}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.OptimizationKeyType, U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}, E, N}","page":"Internals","text":"_add_container!(\n    opt_container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.OptimizationKeyType},\n    ::Type{U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}},\n    ::Type{E},\n    sparse::Bool,\n    axs...;\n    meta\n) -> Any\n\n\nKey-constructing overload: builds the key from (T, U, meta) then delegates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_container!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_mccormick_envelope!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Float64, Float64, Float64, Float64, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_mccormick_envelope!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    z_var,\n    x_min::Float64,\n    x_max::Float64,\n    y_min::Float64,\n    y_max::Float64,\n    meta::String;\n    lower_bounds\n)\n\n\n_add_mccormick_envelope!(container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, z_var, x_min, x_max, y_min, y_max, meta)\n\nAdd McCormick envelope constraints for the bilinear product z ≈ x·y.\n\nFor each (name, t), adds 4 linear inequalities:\n\nz ≥ x_min·y + x·y_min − x_min·y_min\nz ≥ x_max·y + x·y_max − x_max·y_max\nz ≤ x_max·y + x·y_min − x_max·y_min\nz ≤ x_min·y + x·y_max − x_min·y_max\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of x variables indexed by (name, t)\ny_var: container of y variables indexed by (name, t)\nz_var: container of z variables indexed by (name, t)\nx_min::Float64: lower bound of x\nx_max::Float64: upper bound of x\ny_min::Float64: lower bound of y\ny_max::Float64: upper bound of y\nmeta::String: identifier for container keys\n\nReturns\n\nNothing. Constraints are added in-place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_mccormick_envelope!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_mccormick_envelope!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_mccormick_envelope!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    z_var,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String;\n    lower_bounds\n)\n\n\n_add_mccormick_envelope!(container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, z_var, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nAdd McCormick envelope constraints for the bilinear product z ≈ x·y with per-name bounds.\n\nFor each (name, t), adds 4 linear inequalities using bounds looked up by name index.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of x variables indexed by (name, t)\ny_var: container of y variables indexed by (name, t)\nz_var: container of z variables indexed by (name, t)\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\nmeta::String: identifier for container keys\n\nReturns\n\nNothing. Constraints are added in-place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_mccormick_envelope!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_pwl_constraint_compact!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, T, String, Vector{Float64}, SOSStatusVariable, Int64, JuMP.VariableRef, Float64}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, T, String, Vector{Float64}, SOSStatusVariable, Int64, JuMP.VariableRef, Float64, Bool}} where T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_pwl_constraint_compact!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    name::String,\n    break_points::Vector{Float64},\n    sos_status::SOSStatusVariable,\n    period::Int64,\n    power_var::JuMP.VariableRef,\n    P_min::Float64\n)\n_add_pwl_constraint_compact!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    name::String,\n    break_points::Vector{Float64},\n    sos_status::SOSStatusVariable,\n    period::Int64,\n    power_var::JuMP.VariableRef,\n    P_min::Float64,\n    must_run::Bool\n)\n\n\nImplement the constraints for PWL variables for Compact form. That is:\n\nsum_kinmathcalK P_k^max delta_kt = p_t + P_min cdot u_t \nsum_kinmathcalK delta_kt = on_t\n\nFor standard form, use _add_pwl_constraint_standard! instead.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_pwl_constraint_compact!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_pwl_constraint_standard!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, T, Vector{Float64}, SOSStatusVariable, Int64, JuMP.VariableRef}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, T, Vector{Float64}, SOSStatusVariable, Int64, JuMP.VariableRef, Bool}} where T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_pwl_constraint_standard!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    break_points::Vector{Float64},\n    sos_status::SOSStatusVariable,\n    period::Int64,\n    power_var::JuMP.VariableRef\n)\n_add_pwl_constraint_standard!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    break_points::Vector{Float64},\n    sos_status::SOSStatusVariable,\n    period::Int64,\n    power_var::JuMP.VariableRef,\n    must_run::Bool\n)\n\n\nImplement the standard constraints for PWL variables. That is:\n\nsum_kinmathcalK P_k^max delta_kt = p_t \nsum_kinmathcalK delta_kt = on_t\n\nFor compact form (PowerAboveMinimumVariable), use _add_pwl_constraint_compact! instead.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_pwl_constraint_standard!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_pwmcc_concave_cuts!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Int64, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_pwmcc_concave_cuts!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    v_var,\n    q_expr,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    K::Int64,\n    meta::String\n)\n\n\n_add_pwmcc_concave_cuts!(container, C, names, time_steps, v_var, q_expr, bounds, K, meta)\n\nAdd piecewise McCormick cuts on a concave term (-v^2) to tighten its SoS2 LP relaxation.\n\nPartitions each name's [vmin, vmax] into K uniform sub-intervals and adds disaggregated variables, binary interval selectors, and chord/tangent constraints that cut off the interior of the SoS2 relaxation polytope.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nv_var: container of the original variable indexed by (name, t)\nq_expr: expression container for the SoS2 approximation of v^2 (indexed by (name, t))\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of v domain\nK::Int: number of sub-intervals (K=2 is the minimal useful choice)\nmeta::String: unique key prefix, e.g. \"pwmccx\" or \"pwmccy\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_pwmcc_concave_cuts!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(config::DNMDTQuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x² using the Double NMDT (DNMDT) method from raw variable inputs.\n\nDiscretizes x via _discretize! then delegates to the NMDTDiscretization overload. Stores results in a QuadraticExpression container.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::DNMDTQuadConfig: configuration with depth (binary discretization levels) and epigraph_depth (LP tightening depth; 0 to disable, default 3×depth)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(config::DNMDTQuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_disc, bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x² using the Double NMDT (DNMDT) method from a pre-built discretization.\n\nConstructs two binary-continuous products (β·xh and β·δ) and delegates to the core DNMDT assembler, storing results in a QuadraticExpression container. Optionally tightens lower bounds with an epigraph relaxation via _tighten_lower_bounds!.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::DNMDTQuadConfig: configuration with depth (binary discretization levels) and epigraph_depth (LP tightening depth; 0 to disable, default 3×depth)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_disc::NMDTDiscretization: pre-built discretization for x\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphQuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphQuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(::EpigraphQuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nCreate a variable z that lower-bounds x² using the sawtooth-epigraph Q^{L1} relaxation (Beach, Burlacu, Hager, Hildebrand 2024, Definition 6).\n\nFor each (name, t), creates a variable z, the sawtooth aux variables g0, …, gL with g_j ≤ 2·g_{j-1} and g_j ≤ 2·(1 − g_{j-1}), the linking constraint g_0 = (x − x_min)/Δ, and L + 1 sawtooth-encoded tangent cuts z ≥ fʲ(x, g) − 2^{-2j-2} for j = 0, …, L, plus the two boundary tangents to x² at x = xmin and x = xmax. Pure LP — zero binary variables.\n\nStores affine expressions that lower-bound x² in an EpigraphExpression expression container.\n\nThe maximum underestimation gap between the tangent envelope and x² is Δ²·2^{−2·depth−4} where Δ = xmax − xmin.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::EpigraphQuadConfig: configuration with depth field L controlling the sawtooth-epigraph relaxation — L + 1 sawtooth-encoded tangent cuts (j = 0, …, L) plus two boundary tangents, for L + 3 tangent constraints total\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: variable type identifier for the approximated variable\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(config::ManualSOS2QuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x² using a piecewise linear function with manually-implemented SOS2 constraints.\n\nCreates lambda (λ) variables representing convex combination weights over breakpoints, adds linking, normalization, and manual adjacency constraints using binary variables, and stores affine expressions approximating x² in a QuadraticExpression expression container.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::ManualSOS2QuadConfig: configuration with depth (number of PWL segments) and pwmcc_segments (PWMCC cut partitions; 0 to disable, default 0)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: variable type identifier for the approximation (allows multiple approximations per component type)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(config::NMDTQuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x² using the NMDT method from raw variable inputs.\n\nDiscretizes x via _discretize! then delegates to the NMDTDiscretization overload. Stores results in a QuadraticExpression container.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::NMDTQuadConfig: configuration with depth (binary discretization levels) and epigraph_depth (LP tightening depth; 0 to disable, default 3×depth)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(config::NMDTQuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_disc, bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x² using the NMDT method from a pre-built discretization.\n\nComputes the binary-continuous product β·xh and residual product δ·xh, then assembles x² via _assemble_product!. Stores results in a QuadraticExpression container. Optionally tightens lower bounds with an epigraph relaxation.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::NMDTQuadConfig: configuration with depth (binary discretization levels) and epigraph_depth (LP tightening depth; 0 to disable, default 3×depth)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_disc::NMDTDiscretization: pre-built discretization for x\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoQuadApproxConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    _::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NoQuadApproxConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(::NoQuadApproxConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nNo-op quadratic approximation: returns exact x² as a QuadExpr.\n\nArguments\n\n::NoQuadApproxConfig: no-op configuration (no fields)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: variable type identifier for the approximation\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(config::SawtoothQuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x² using the sawtooth MIP formulation.\n\nCreates auxiliary continuous variables g0,...,gL and binary variables α1,...,αL, adds S^L constraints (4 per level) and a linking constraint for each component and time step, and stores affine expressions approximating x² in a QuadraticExpression expression container.\n\nFor depth L, the approximation interpolates x² at 2^L + 1 uniformly spaced breakpoints with maximum overestimation error Δ² · 2^{-2L-2} where Δ = xmax - xmin.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::SawtoothQuadConfig: configuration with depth (recursion depth L; uses L binary variables) and epigraph_depth (LP tightening depth; 0 to disable)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: variable type identifier for the approximation (allows multiple approximations per component type)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig, OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_quadratic_approx!(\n    config::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_add_quadratic_approx!(config::SolverSOS2QuadConfig, container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nApproximate x² using a piecewise linear function with solver-native SOS2 constraints.\n\nCreates lambda_var (λ) variables representing convex combination weights over breakpoints, adds linking, normalization, and MOI.SOS2 constraints, and stores affine expressions approximating x² in a QuadraticExpression expression container.\n\nArguments\n\nconfig::SolverSOS2QuadConfig: configuration with depth (number of PWL segments) and pwmcc_segments (PWMCC cut partitions; 0 to disable, default 0)\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: variable type identifier for the approximation (allows multiple approximations per component type)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_quadratic_approx!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_reformulated_mccormick!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_add_reformulated_mccormick!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    y_var,\n    psq,\n    xsq,\n    ysq,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n)\n\n\n_add_reformulated_mccormick!(container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, y_var, psq, xsq, ysq, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta)\n\nAdd 4 reformulated McCormick cuts for Bin2 separable bilinear approximation. Substitutes z = ½(zp1 − zx − z_y) into the standard McCormick envelope.\n\npsq, xsq, ysq are expression containers for (x+y)², x², y² approximations.\n\nArguments\n\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of y\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_reformulated_mccormick!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_ts_incremental_pwl_cost!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{D, OptimizationContainer, C, Type{T}, Type{U}, InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem, Float64}} where {D<:InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OfferDirection, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, T<:VariableType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"_add_ts_incremental_pwl_cost!(\n    dir::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.OfferDirection,\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    power_units::InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem,\n    device_base_power::Float64\n)\n\n\nPSY-free delta PWL objective formulation for time-series-backed incremental value curves. Reads slopes/breakpoints from parameter containers populated externally. All parameter array lookups and buffer allocations are hoisted before the time loop to avoid repeated dictionary lookups and allocations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_ts_incremental_pwl_cost!"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_vom_cost_to_objective!","page":"Internals","text":"_add_vom_cost_to_objective!(container, ::Type{VariableType}, component, op_cost, ::Type{Formulation})\n\nAdd the variable operations & maintenance (VOM) cost term. POM provides the method dispatching on PSY.OfferCurveCost.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._add_vom_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_dnmdt!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Any, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Int64, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_assemble_dnmdt!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    bx_yh_expr,\n    by_dx_expr,\n    by_xh_expr,\n    bx_dy_expr,\n    x_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    y_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    depth::Int64,\n    meta::String;\n    lambda,\n    result_type,\n    tighten\n) -> Any\n\n\n_assemble_dnmdt!(container, C, names, time_steps, bx_yh_expr, by_dx_expr, by_xh_expr, bx_dy_expr, x_disc, y_disc, meta; lambda, result_type)\n\nCore assembler for the DNMDT bilinear approximation of x·y from pre-computed cross products.\n\nBuilds two NMDT product estimates from opposite discretization pairings and combines them:\n\nz₁ = assemble(bx·yh + by·δx + δx·δy, xdisc, ydisc)\nz₂ = assemble(by·xh + bx·δy + δx·δy, ydisc, xdisc)\nresult = λ·z₁ + (1−λ)·z₂\n\nThe shared residual product δx·δy is computed internally. Stores results in an expression container of type result_type.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nbx_yh_expr: expression for β_x·yh binary-continuous products\nby_dx_expr: expression for β_y·δx binary-continuous products\nby_xh_expr: expression for β_y·xh binary-continuous products\nbx_dy_expr: expression for β_x·δy binary-continuous products\nx_disc::NMDTDiscretization: discretization for x\ny_disc::NMDTDiscretization: discretization for y\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name bounds for x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name bounds for y\ndepth::Int: number of binary discretization levels L\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\nlambda::Float64: convex combination weight for the two NMDT estimates (default: DNMDT_LAMBDA = 0.5)\nresult_type: expression type to store results in (default: NMDTResultExpression)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_dnmdt!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_product!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_assemble_product!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    terms,\n    dz_var,\n    xh_expr,\n    yh_expr,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String;\n    result_type\n) -> Any\n\n\n_assemble_product!(container, C, names, time_steps, terms, dz_var, xh_norm, yh_norm, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta; result_type)\n\nReconstruct the bilinear product x·y from normalized NMDT components.\n\nApplies the affine rescaling:\n\nx·y = lx·ly·zh + lx·y_min·xh + ly·x_min·yh + x_min·y_min\n\nwhere zh = Σ terms[name,t] + dz_var[name,t] collects the binary-continuous and residual product contributions, lx = xmax − xmin, ly = ymax − ymin.\n\nStores results in an expression container of type result_type.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nterms: iterable of expression containers indexed by (name, t) for the binary-continuous products\ndz_var: variable container for the residual product δ·y\nxh_norm: normed expression container for x\nyh_norm: normed expression container for y\nx_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name bounds for x\ny_bounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name bounds for y\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\nresult_type: expression type to store results in (default: NMDTResultExpression)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_product!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_product!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_assemble_product!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    terms,\n    dz_var,\n    x_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    yh_expr,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String;\n    result_type\n) -> Any\n\n\n_assemble_product!(container, C, names, time_steps, terms, dz_var, x_disc::NMDTDiscretization, yh_expr, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta; result_type)\n\nConvenience overload: extracts norm_expr from xdisc and delegates to the core `assemble_product!`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_product!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_product!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_assemble_product!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    terms,\n    dz_var,\n    x_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    y_disc::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization,\n    x_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    y_bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String;\n    result_type\n) -> Any\n\n\n_assemble_product!(container, C, names, time_steps, terms, dz_var, x_disc::NMDTDiscretization, y_disc::NMDTDiscretization, x_bounds, y_bounds, meta; result_type)\n\nConvenience overload: extracts norm_expr from both discretizations and delegates to the core _assemble_product!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._assemble_product!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._binary_continuous_product!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Float64, Float64, Int64, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_binary_continuous_product!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    bin_disc,\n    cont_var,\n    cont_min::Float64,\n    cont_max::Float64,\n    depth::Int64,\n    meta::String;\n    tighten\n) -> Any\n\n\n_binary_continuous_product!(container, C, names, time_steps, bin_disc, cont_var, cont_min, cont_max, depth, meta; tighten)\n\nLinearize each binary-continuous product β_i·y using McCormick envelopes.\n\nFor each depth level i, creates a variable ui ≈ βi·y with bounds [contmin, contmax] and adds 4 McCormick constraints via _add_mccormick_envelope!. Assembles the weighted sum Σᵢ 2^{−i}·u_i into a NMDTBinaryContinuousProductExpression.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nbin_disc: NMDTDiscretization providing β_i variables and depth\ncont_var: container of continuous variables y indexed by (name, t)\ncont_min::Float64: lower bound of y\ncont_max::Float64: upper bound of y\ndepth::Int: number of binary discretization levels\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\ntighten::Bool: if true, omit McCormick lower bounds (for use when a tighter bound is applied elsewhere)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._binary_continuous_product!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._block_width_constraint-Tuple{Type{PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOfferConstraint}}","page":"Internals","text":"_block_width_constraint(\n    _::Type{PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalOfferConstraint}\n) -> Type{PiecewiseLinearBlockIncrementalWidthConstraint}\n\n\nMap a block-offer linking-constraint type to its paired block-width constraint type.\n\nMirrors the direction-keyed _block_width_constraint mapping in value_curve_cost.jl, but keyed on the offer-constraint type itself so add_pwl_constraint_delta! can resolve the width type from its existing ::Type{W} argument without a new parameter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._block_width_constraint"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._ceil_positive-Tuple{Float64}","page":"Internals","text":"_ceil_positive(x::Float64) -> Int64\n\n\n_ceil_positive(x::Float64)::Int\n\nSmallest integer ≥ x, clamped to ≥ 1. Used by every tolerance_depth helper to convert a real-valued depth bound (e.g. log₂(Δ²/τ)/2) into a usable depth. Guards against non-finite x (which would otherwise throw an opaque InexactError from ceil(Int, Inf)).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._ceil_positive"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._check_container_dims-Tuple{OptimizationContainerKey, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_check_container_dims(key::OptimizationContainerKey, value)\n\n\nReject 1D dense/sparse JuMP containers (issue #15): variable/constraint/expression/dual containers must always be indexable as x[i, j], never as a bare vector x[i]. Containers with 3+ dimensions (e.g. PWL sparse containers keyed on (name, segment, time)) are fine.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._check_container_dims"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._check_tolerance_args-Tuple{Float64, Vararg{Float64}}","page":"Internals","text":"_check_tolerance_args(\n    tolerance::Float64,\n    deltas::Float64...\n)\n\n\n_check_tolerance_args(tolerance::Float64, deltas::Float64...)\n\nValidate the common arguments of every tolerance_depth helper. Throws an informative ArgumentError if tolerance or any domain length in deltas is not strictly positive, so callers get a clear message instead of a low-level DomainError/InexactError surfacing from sqrt/log2/ceil.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._check_tolerance_args"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._discretize!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Int64, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_discretize!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    depth::Int64,\n    meta::String\n) -> InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTDiscretization\n\n\n_discretize!(container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, depth, meta)\n\nDiscretize the normalized variable xh = (x − xmin)/(xmax − x_min) using L binary variables.\n\nCreates L binary variables β₁,…,βL and one residual δ ∈ [0, 2^{−L}] such that xh = Σᵢ 2^{−i}·βi + δ. Enforces this via a NMDTEDiscretizationConstraint and returns an NMDTDiscretization struct holding all components.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\ndepth::Int: number of binary discretization levels L\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._discretize!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._fill_pwl_data_from_arrays!-Tuple{Vector{Float64}, Vector{Float64}, JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N, JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N, JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N, JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N, UnitRange{Int64}, UnitRange{Int64}, String, Int64, InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem, Float64, Float64}","page":"Internals","text":"_fill_pwl_data_from_arrays!(\n    slopes::Vector{Float64},\n    breakpoints::Vector{Float64},\n    slope_arr::JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N,\n    slope_mult::JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N,\n    bp_arr::JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N,\n    bp_mult::JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{Float64, N} where N,\n    seg_axis::UnitRange{Int64},\n    point_axis::UnitRange{Int64},\n    name::String,\n    time::Int64,\n    power_units::InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem,\n    model_base_power::Float64,\n    device_base_power::Float64\n)\n\n\nFill pre-allocated slope and breakpoint buffers from parameter arrays for a single time step. Reads raw values from parameter arrays, then applies unit conversion via get_piecewise_curve_per_system_unit.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._fill_pwl_data_from_arrays!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_entry-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, OptimizationContainerKey{T, U}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.OptimizationKeyType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsType}","page":"Internals","text":"_get_entry(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    key::OptimizationContainerKey{T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.OptimizationKeyType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsType}\n) -> Any\n\n\nGeneric container entry getter. Dispatches on key type to access the correct field. Replaces per-type getvariable, getauxvariable, getconstraint, etc. by key.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_entry-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{U}, Any}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.OptimizationKeyType, U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}}","page":"Internals","text":"_get_entry(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.OptimizationKeyType},\n    ::Type{U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}}\n) -> Any\n_get_entry(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    #s361::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.OptimizationKeyType},\n    #s360::Type{U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}},\n    meta\n) -> Any\n\n\nGeneric container entry getter by entry type and component type. Constructs the appropriate key and delegates to the key-based getentry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_initial_condition_type-Tuple{Type{<:ConstraintType}, Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}, Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}}","page":"Internals","text":"_get_initial_condition_type(\n    X::Type{<:ConstraintType},\n    Y::Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    Z::Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: get the initial condition type for a given constraint, device, and formulation. Concrete implementations in POM. Used for ramp constraints.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_initial_condition_type"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_parameter_field","page":"Internals","text":"_get_parameter_field(::Type{<:ParameterType}, op_cost)\n\nExtract the raw field corresponding to this parameter type from an operation cost object. POM provides overloads.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_parameter_field"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_pwl_data","page":"Internals","text":"_get_pwl_data(direction, container, component, time)\n\nReturn (breakpoints, slopes) for the given component at the given time step, ready for unit conversion. POM's static-curve overload forwards to _get_raw_pwl_data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_pwl_data"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_raw_pwl_data","page":"Internals","text":"_get_raw_pwl_data(direction, container, ComponentType, name, cost_data, time)\n\nReturn (breakpoint_cost, slope_cost, unit_system). The IS-backed TS method lives here in IOM; the static CostCurve{PiecewiseIncrementalCurve} method is provided by POM.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._get_raw_pwl_data"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._handle_natural_units-Tuple{DataFrame, Float64, OptimizationContainerKey}","page":"Internals","text":"_handle_natural_units(\n    df::DataFrame,\n    base_power::Float64,\n    key::OptimizationContainerKey\n) -> DataFrame\n\n\nConvert the value column to natural units, if required by the key. Does not mutate the input dataframe.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._handle_natural_units"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._is_time_series_cost-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_is_time_series_cost(_) -> Bool\n\n\nPredicate: is this op_cost time-series-backed? POM extends for TS types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._is_time_series_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._make_bound_constraint-Tuple{LowerBound, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_make_bound_constraint(\n    _::LowerBound,\n    model,\n    lhs,\n    rhs\n) -> JuMP.ConstraintRef{M, C} where {M<:JuMP.GenericModel, C<:MathOptInterface.ConstraintIndex}\n\n\nCreate a bound constraint with the appropriate direction.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._make_bound_constraint"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._mc_setindex!-Union{Tuple{B}, Tuple{A}, Tuple{Any, Tuple{A, B}, Int64, Any}} where {A, B}","page":"Internals","text":"_mc_setindex!(\n    cons,\n    index::Tuple{A, B},\n    n::Int64,\n    constraint\n) -> Any\n\n\n_mc_setindex!(cons, index, n, constraint)\n\nHelper function for setting constraints by-index in a McCormick constraint container.\n\nSupports 2- and 3-length tuples.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._mc_setindex!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._normed_variable!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_normed_variable!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_var,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    meta::String\n) -> Any\n\n\n_normed_variable!(container, C, names, time_steps, x_var, bounds, meta)\n\nCreate an affine expression for the normalized variable xh = (x − xmin) / (xmax − x_min) ∈ [0,1].\n\nStores results in a NormedVariableExpression expression container.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_var: container of variables indexed by (name, t)\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of x domain\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._normed_variable!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._rebuild_with_value_curve-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_rebuild_with_value_curve(\n    c::InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve,\n    vc\n) -> InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve\n\n\nCreates piecewise linear cost function using a sum of variables and expression with sign and time step included.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nvar_key::VariableKey: The variable name\ncomponentname::String: The componentname of the variable container\ncost_function::Union{IS.CostCurve{IS.PiecewiseIncrementalCurve}, IS.CostCurve{IS.PiecewiseAverageCurve}}: container for piecewise linear cost\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._rebuild_with_value_curve"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._residual_product!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Float64, Int64, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_residual_product!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    x_disc,\n    y_var,\n    y_max::Float64,\n    depth::Int64,\n    meta::String;\n    tighten\n) -> Any\n\n\n_residual_product!(container, C, names, time_steps, x_disc, y_var, y_max, meta; tighten)\n\nLinearize the residual-continuous product z ≈ δ·y using McCormick envelopes.\n\nCreates a variable z ∈ [0, 2^{−L}·y_max] for each (name, t) and bounds it with McCormick constraints on (δ, y) where δ ∈ [0, 2^{−L}]. Stores results in a NMDTResidualProductVariable container.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nx_disc: NMDTDiscretization for x, providing delta_var and depth\ny_var: container of continuous variables y indexed by (name, t)\ny_max::Float64: upper bound of y (lower bound assumed 0)\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\ntighten::Bool: if true, omit McCormick lower bounds (default: false)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._residual_product!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._sanitize_model_name-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_sanitize_model_name(name::AbstractString) -> String\n\n\nSanitize a model name for use as a filesystem path component. Replaces path separators, null bytes, and control characters with underscores.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._sanitize_model_name"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._square-Tuple{Float64}","page":"Internals","text":"_square(x::Float64) -> Float64\n\n\nHelper: returns x² (used as the default function for PWL breakpoint generation).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._square"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._summary_to_dict!-Tuple{OptimizerStats, JuMP.Model}","page":"Internals","text":"_summary_to_dict!(\n    optimizer_stats::OptimizerStats,\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model\n)\n\n\nRun this function only when getting detailed solver stats\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._summary_to_dict!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._template_has_outage_aware_branch-Tuple{Dict{Symbol, DeviceModel}}","page":"Internals","text":"_template_has_outage_aware_branch(\n    branch_models::Dict{Symbol, DeviceModel}\n) -> Bool\n\n\nTrue if any branch DeviceModel in branch_models uses a formulation that consumes DeviceModel.outages (per supports_outages). POM's AbstractSecurityConstrainedStaticBranch specialization makes that trait return true; non-SC formulations default to false.\n\nBranchModelContainer (Dict{Symbol, DeviceModelForBranches}) is defined at the top of this file and exported from IOM.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._template_has_outage_aware_branch"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._tighten_lower_bounds!-Union{Tuple{C}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{C}, Vector{String}, UnitRange{Int64}, Any, Any, Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}}, Int64, String}} where C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent","page":"Internals","text":"_tighten_lower_bounds!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names::Vector{String},\n    time_steps::UnitRange{Int64},\n    result_expr,\n    x_disc,\n    bounds::Vector{@NamedTuple{min::Float64, max::Float64}},\n    epigraph_depth::Int64,\n    meta::String\n)\n\n\n_tighten_lower_bounds!(container, C, names, time_steps, result_expr, x_disc, epigraph_depth, meta)\n\nAdd epigraph lower-bound constraints to tighten an NMDT quadratic approximation.\n\nComputes an epigraph Q^{L1} lower bound on xh² and adds a NMDTTightenConstraint enforcing result_expr[name,t] ≥ epi_expr[name,t] for each (name, t). This improves the lower bound quality of NMDT without adding binaries.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: the optimization container\n::Type{C}: component type\nnames::Vector{String}: component names\ntime_steps::UnitRange{Int}: time periods\nresult_expr: expression container for the NMDT quadratic result to be tightened\nx_disc: NMDTDiscretization for x, providing norm_expr and depth\nbounds::Vector{MinMax}: per-name lower and upper bounds of the x domain, used to unnormalize the epigraph cut from the normalized frame xh ∈ [0,1] to original units\nepigraph_depth::Int: depth for the epigraph Q^{L1} lower-bound approximation\nmeta::String: identifier encoding the original variable type being approximated\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._tighten_lower_bounds!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._to_is_interval-Tuple{Dates.Millisecond}","page":"Internals","text":"_to_is_interval(\n    interval::Dates.Millisecond\n) -> Union{Nothing, Dates.Millisecond}\n\n\nConvert the internal Dates.Millisecond interval (where UNSET_INTERVAL means unset) to the Union{Nothing, Dates.Period} form the IS / PSY time-series API expects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._to_is_interval"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._to_is_resolution-Tuple{Dates.Millisecond}","page":"Internals","text":"_to_is_resolution(\n    resolution::Dates.Millisecond\n) -> Union{Nothing, Dates.Millisecond}\n\n\nConvert the internal Dates.Millisecond resolution (where UNSET_RESOLUTION means unset) to the Union{Nothing, Dates.Period} form the IS / PSY time-series API expects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._to_is_resolution"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._validate_eltype-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesKey}, Tuple{Type{T}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesKey, Any}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"_validate_eltype(\n    ::Type{T},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    ts_key::InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesKey\n) -> Any\n_validate_eltype(\n    ::Type{T},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    ts_key::InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesKey,\n    msg\n) -> Any\n\n\nValidate that the eltype of the time series, or the field itself if it's not a time series, is of the type given\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._validate_eltype"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels._vom_offer_direction","page":"Internals","text":"Default: most formulations use incremental offers. POM overrides for loads.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels._vom_offer_direction"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_parameters!-Union{Tuple{W}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, U, DeviceModelForBranches{D, W}}} where {D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, T<:ParameterType, U<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D}, Vector{D}}, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_parameters!(\n    _::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:ParameterType},\n    devices::Union{Array{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    model::DeviceModel{D<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, W<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Add parameters to the optimization container. Concrete implementations are in PowerOperationsModels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_parameters!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_cost!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{U}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{T}, Vector{T}}, Type{V}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, U<:VariableType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_proportional_cost!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{U<:VariableType},\n    devices::Union{Array{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    _::Type{V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nDefault implementation for proportional cost, where the cost term is not time variant. See also: add_proportional_cost_maybe_time_variant! for a common basis for devices that might have time-variant proportional costs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_cost!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_cost_invariant!-Union{Tuple{E}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, C, Float64, InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem, Float64, Type{E}}} where {T<:VariableType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, E<:CostExpressions}","page":"Internals","text":"add_proportional_cost_invariant!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_term::Float64,\n    power_units::InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem,\n    multiplier::Float64,\n    _::Type{E<:CostExpressions}\n)\n\n\nAdd a proportional (linear) cost to the invariant objective across all time steps.\n\nNormalizes cost_term from power_units to system per-unit, multiplies by dt and multiplier, then adds variable * rate to the target expression E and the invariant objective for each time step.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer: the optimization container\nT: variable type (caller provides)\ncomponent: the component (used for name, base power, and variable lookup)\ncost_term: raw proportional cost (e.g., /MWh before normalization)\npower_units: unit system of cost_term\nmultiplier: additional scalar (e.g., objective_function_multiplier, fuel cost)\nE: target cost expression type (e.g., FuelCostExpression, VOMCostExpression). Constituent types auto-propagate into ProductionCostExpression via _propagate_to_production_cost!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_cost_invariant!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_cost_maybe_time_variant!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{U}, Union{InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{T}, Vector{T}}, Type{V}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, U<:VariableType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_proportional_cost_maybe_time_variant!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{U<:VariableType},\n    devices::Union{Array{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, 1}, InfrastructureSystems.FlattenIteratorWrapper{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}},\n    _::Type{V<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nCommon basis for maybe time variant proportional costs for devices that might have must-run behavior. Currently used for (ThermalGen, AbstractThermal) and (ControllableLoad, PowerLoadInterruption) device, formulation pairs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_proportional_cost_maybe_time_variant!"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_block_offer_constraints!","page":"Internals","text":"add_pwl_block_offer_constraints!(\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    con_container,\n    width_container,\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    power_var::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    pwl_vars::Vector{JuMP.VariableRef},\n    breakpoints::Vector{<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}}\n)\nadd_pwl_block_offer_constraints!(\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    con_container,\n    width_container,\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    power_var::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    pwl_vars::Vector{JuMP.VariableRef},\n    breakpoints::Vector{<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}},\n    min_power_offset::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}\n)\n\n\nAdd block-offer PWL constraints: linking constraint and per-block upper bounds.\n\npower_var == Σ δ[k] + min_power_offset\nδ[k] <= breakpoints[k+1] - breakpoints[k]   for each k\n\nArguments\n\njump_model: the JuMP model\ncon_container: constraint container to store the linking constraint (indexed [name, t])\nwidth_container: sparse constraint container to store each per-block width row,  keyed (name, block, t)\nname: component name\nt: time period\npower_var: the power variable being linked\npwl_vars: vector of block-offer delta variables (length = n_blocks)\nbreakpoints: vector of breakpoint values (length = n_blocks + 1)\nmin_power_offset: offset for minimum generation power (default 0.0)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_pwl_block_offer_constraints!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_ramp_constraint_pair!-Union{Tuple{S}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{JuMP.Model, @NamedTuple{up::C, down::C}, String, Int64, @NamedTuple{up::V, down::V}, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, @NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}, Number, @NamedTuple{up::S, down::S}}, Tuple{JuMP.Model, @NamedTuple{up::C, down::C}, String, Int64, @NamedTuple{up::V, down::V}, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, @NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}, Number, @NamedTuple{up::S, down::S}, Bool}} where {C, V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}}","page":"Internals","text":"add_ramp_constraint_pair!(\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    cons::@NamedTuple{up::C, down::C},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    current::@NamedTuple{up::V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, down::V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}},\n    previous::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    limits::@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64},\n    dt::Number,\n    slack::@NamedTuple{up::S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, down::S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}}\n)\nadd_ramp_constraint_pair!(\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    cons::@NamedTuple{up::C, down::C},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    current::@NamedTuple{up::V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, down::V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}},\n    previous::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    limits::@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64},\n    dt::Number,\n    slack::@NamedTuple{up::S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, down::S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}},\n    bound_decrease::Bool\n)\n\n\nAdd a pair of ramp-up and ramp-down constraints for a single (name, t).\n\nRamp up:   current.up - previous <= limits.up * dt + slack.up\nRamp down (bound_decrease=true, default):\n           previous - current.down <= limits.down * dt + slack.down\nRamp down (bound_decrease=false):\n            previous - current.down + slack.down >= - limits.down * dt\n    equivalent to: current.down - previous <= limits.down * dt + slack.down\n        i.e. we're actually bounding the increase not the decrease.\n        (the lower bound represents something different in the Expression case)\n\nWhen bound_decrease = false (default), the down constraint mirrors the up constraint direction, bounding how much power can increase from the previous value (using the down ramp rate). When bound_decrease = true, the down constraint flips current and previous, bounding how much power can decrease.\n\nArguments\n\njump_model: the JuMP model\ncons: UpDownPair of constraint containers (up=, down=)\nname: component name\nt: time period\ncurrent: UpDownPair of current values (up=, down=); use same value for both if not using expressions\nprevious: previous timestep value (ic_power for t=1, variable[t-1] for t>1)\nlimits: UpDown (Float64) ramp limits\ndt: minutes per period\nslack: UpDownPair of slack variables\nbound_decrease: if false, flip current/previous in down constraint (default: true)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_ramp_constraint_pair!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_ramp_constraint_startstop_pair!-Union{Tuple{R}, Tuple{S}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{JuMP.Model, @NamedTuple{up::C, down::C}, String, Int64, @NamedTuple{up::V, down::V}, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, @NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}, Number, @NamedTuple{up::R, down::R}, @NamedTuple{up::S, down::S}}} where {C, V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, R<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}}","page":"Internals","text":"add_ramp_constraint_startstop_pair!(\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    cons::@NamedTuple{up::C, down::C},\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    current::@NamedTuple{up::V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, down::V<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}},\n    previous::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    limits::@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64},\n    dt::Number,\n    startstop::@NamedTuple{up::R<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, down::R<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}},\n    slack::@NamedTuple{up::S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, down::S<:Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}}\n)\n\n\nAdd a pair of ramp-up and ramp-down constraints with start/stop condition terms.\n\nLike add_ramp_constraint_pair!, but includes start/stop condition terms that relax the ramp limits when a unit is starting up or shutting down.\n\nRamp up:   current.up - previous <= limits.up * dt + slack.up + startstop.up\nRamp down: previous - current.down <= limits.down * dt + slack.down + startstop.down\n\nArguments\n\njump_model: the JuMP model\ncons: UpDownPair of constraint containers (up=, down=)\nname: component name\nt: time period\ncurrent: UpDownPair of current values (up=, down=); use same value for both if not using expressions\nprevious: previous timestep value (ic_power for t=1, variable[t-1] for t>1)\nlimits: UpDown (Float64) ramp limits\ndt: minutes per period\nstartstop: UpDownPair of start/stop condition terms\nslack: UpDownPair of slack variables\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_ramp_constraint_startstop_pair!"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_range_bound_constraint!","page":"Internals","text":"add_range_bound_constraint!(\n    dir::BoundDirection,\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    con_container,\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    variable::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    bound::Float64\n)\nadd_range_bound_constraint!(\n    dir::BoundDirection,\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    con_container,\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    variable::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    bound::Float64,\n    binary_var::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}\n)\n\n\nAdd a range bound constraint.\n\nLowerBound: variable >= bound * binary_var\nUpperBound: variable <= bound * binary_var\n\nWhen binary_var = 1.0 (default), this is a simple bound constraint. When binary_var is a JuMP variable, this is a semicontinuous constraint.\n\nArguments\n\ndir: LowerBound() or UpperBound()\njump_model: the JuMP model\ncon_container: constraint container (DenseAxisArray or SparseAxisArray)\nname: component name\nt: time period\nvariable: the variable or expression to constrain\nbound: the bound value\nbinary_var: multiplier for semicontinuous constraints (default: 1.0)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_range_bound_constraint!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_range_equality_constraint!-Tuple{JuMP.Model, Any, String, Int64, Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar}, Float64}","page":"Internals","text":"add_range_equality_constraint!(\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    con_container,\n    name::String,\n    t::Int64,\n    variable::Union{Float64, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar},\n    value::Float64\n)\n\n\nAdd an equality constraint.\n\nvariable == value\n\nUse this for the fixed-value case when min ≈ max.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_range_equality_constraint!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_updown_constraints_containers!-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, Type{V}, Any, Any}} where {T<:ConstraintType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Internals","text":"add_updown_constraints_containers!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    names,\n    time_steps\n) -> NamedTuple{(:up, :down), <:Tuple{Any, Any}}\n\n\nCreate paired up/down constraint containers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_updown_constraints_containers!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.LinearCurve}, Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}}} where T<:VariableType","page":"Internals","text":"add_variable_cost_to_objective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.LinearCurve},\n    _::Type{<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nAdds to the cost function cost terms for sum of variables with common factor to be used for cost expression for optimization_container model.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nvar_key::VariableKey: The variable name\ncomponentname::String: The componentname of the variable container\ncost_component::IS.FuelCurve{IS.LinearCurve} : container for cost to be associated with variable\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, C, InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{<:InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesPiecewiseIncrementalCurve}, Type{U}}} where {T<:VariableType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_variable_cost_to_objective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    ::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{<:InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesPiecewiseIncrementalCurve},\n    ::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation};\n    dir\n)\n\n\nadd_variable_cost_to_objective!(container, ::T, component, cost_function, ::U; dir)\n\nObjective function dispatch for CostCurve{IS.TimeSeriesPiecewiseIncrementalCurve}. Routes to the PSY-free delta PWL formulation that reads from parameter containers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, C, InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve}, Type{U}}} where {T<:VariableType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_variable_cost_to_objective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve},\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nCreates piecewise linear cost function using a sum of variables and expression with sign and time step included.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nvar_key::VariableKey: The variable name\ncomponentname::String: The componentname of the variable container\ncost_function::IS.CostCurve{IS.PiecewisePointCurve}: container for piecewise linear cost\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.LinearCurve}, Type{U}}} where {T<:VariableType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_variable_cost_to_objective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.LinearCurve},\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nAdds to the cost function cost terms for sum of variables with common factor to be used for cost expression for optimization_container model.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nvar_key::VariableKey: The variable name\ncomponentname::String: The componentname of the variable container\ncost_component::IS.CostCurve{IS.LinearCurve} : container for cost to be associated with variable\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.QuadraticCurve}, Type{U}}} where {T<:VariableType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_variable_cost_to_objective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.QuadraticCurve},\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nAdds to the cost function cost terms for sum of variables with common factor to be used for cost expression for optimization_container model.\n\nEquation\n\ngen_cost = dt*sign*(sum(variable.^2)*cost_data[1] + sum(variable)*cost_data[2])\n\nLaTeX\n\ncost = dttimes sign (sum_iin I c_1 v_i^2 + sum_iin I c_2 v_i )\n\nfor quadratic factor large enough. If the first term of the quadratic objective is 0.0, adds a linear cost term sum(variable)*cost_data[2]\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nvar_key::VariableKey: The variable name\ncomponentname::String: The componentname of the variable container\ncost_component::IS.CostCurve{IS.QuadraticCurve} : container for quadratic factors\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.QuadraticCurve}, Type{U}}} where {T<:VariableType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_variable_cost_to_objective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.QuadraticCurve},\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nAdds to the cost function cost terms for sum of variables with common factor to be used for cost expression for optimization_container model.\n\nEquation\n\ngen_cost = dt*(sum(variable.^2)*cost_data[1]*fuel_cost + sum(variable)*cost_data[2]*fuel_cost)\n\nLaTeX\n\ncost = dttimes  (sum_iin I c_f c_1 v_i^2 + sum_iin I c_f c_2 v_i )\n\nfor quadratic factor large enough. If the first term of the quadratic objective is 0.0, adds a linear cost term sum(variable)*cost_data[2]\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nvar_key::VariableKey: The variable name\ncomponentname::String: The componentname of the variable container\ncost_component::IS.FuelCurve{IS.QuadraticCurve} : container for quadratic factors\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!-Union{Tuple{U}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{T}, V, InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve}, Type{U}}} where {T<:VariableType, V<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"add_variable_cost_to_objective!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    cost_function::InfrastructureSystems.FuelCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewisePointCurve},\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nCreates piecewise linear cost function using a sum of variables and expression with sign and time step included.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nvar_key::VariableKey: The variable name\ncomponentname::String: The componentname of the variable container\ncost_function::IS.FuelCurve{IS.PiecewisePointCurve}: container for piecewise linear cost\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.add_variable_cost_to_objective!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.apply_maybe_across_time_series-Tuple{Function, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesKey}","page":"Internals","text":"apply_maybe_across_time_series(\n    fn::Function,\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    ts_key::InfrastructureSystems.TimeSeriesKey\n) -> Any\n\n\nHelper function to look up a time series if necessary then apply a function (typically a validation routine in a do block) to every element in it\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.apply_maybe_across_time_series"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.calculate_aux_variable_value!","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: Calculate auxiliary variable values. Concrete implementations in PowerOperationsModels for specific aux variable types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.calculate_aux_variable_value!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.check_file_integrity-Tuple{String}","page":"Internals","text":"check_file_integrity(path::String)\n\n\ncheck_file_integrity(path::String)\n\nChecks the hash value for each file made with the file is written with the new hash_value to verify the file hasn't been tampered with since written\n\nArguments\n\npath::String: this is the folder path that contains the outputs and the check.sha256 file\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.check_file_integrity"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.component_for_hvdc_interpolation","page":"Internals","text":"Component type associated with hvdc interpolation constraints. Returns DCBus when passed in nothing. Only called in a single spot in incremental.jl.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.component_for_hvdc_interpolation"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.component_for_network_dual","page":"Internals","text":"Component type associated with network duals. Returns ACBus when passed in nothing. Only called in a single spot in add_constraint_dual! for the network model.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.component_for_network_dual"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.constraint_meta-Tuple{LowerBound}","page":"Internals","text":"constraint_meta(_::LowerBound) -> String\n\n\nMeta tag for constraint container (\"lb\" or \"ub\").\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.constraint_meta"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.container_spec-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{Type{Float64}, Vararg{Any, N}}} where N","page":"Internals","text":"container_spec(\n    _::Type{Float64},\n    axs...\n) -> JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray\n\n\nReturns the correct container specification for the selected type of JuMP Model\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.container_spec"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.container_spec-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, Vararg{Any, N}}} where {T, N}","page":"Internals","text":"container_spec(\n    _::Type{T},\n    axs...\n) -> JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray\n\n\nReturns the correct container specification for the selected type of JuMP Model\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.container_spec"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_look_ahead!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{C_dn}, Tuple{C_up}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}}, Matrix{InitialCondition}, Type{C_up}, Type{C_dn}, Type{T}}} where {C_up<:ConstraintType, C_dn<:ConstraintType, T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Internals","text":"device_duration_look_ahead!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    duration_data::Vector{@NamedTuple{up::Float64, down::Float64}},\n    initial_duration::Matrix{InitialCondition},\n    _::Type{C_up<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{C_dn<:ConstraintType},\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}\n)\n\n\nThis formulation of the duration constraints looks ahead in the time frame of the model.\n\nLaTeX\n\nMinimum up-time constraint:\n\nIf t leq d_min^up\n\nd_min^downx_t^stop - sum_i=t-d_min^up + 1^t x_i^on - x_init^up leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps. Otherwise:\n\nd_min^downx_t^stop - sum_i=t-d_min^up + 1^t x_i^on leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nMinimum down-time constraint:\n\nIf t leq d_min^down\n\nd_min^upx_t^start - sum_i=t-d_min^down + 1^t (1 - x_i^on) - x_init^down leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps. Otherwise:\n\nd_min^upx_t^start - sum_i=t-d_min^down + 1^t (1 - x_i^on) leq 0\n\nfor i in the set of time steps.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer : the optimization_container model built in InfrastructureOptimizationModels\nduration_data::Vector{UpDown} : gives how many time steps variable needs to be up or down\ninitial_duration::Matrix{InitialCondition} : gives initial conditions for up (column 1) and down (column 2)\ncons_name::Symbol : name of the constraint\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.device_duration_look_ahead!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.execute_optimizer!-Tuple{OptimizationContainer, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}","page":"Internals","text":"execute_optimizer!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    system::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer\n) -> RunStatus\n\n\nExecute the optimizer on the container's JuMP model, compute aux/dual variables, and return the run status. Called solve_impl!(container, system) in PSI.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.execute_optimizer!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.export_optimizer_stats-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Outputs, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"export_optimizer_stats(\n    res::InfrastructureSystems.Outputs,\n    directory::AbstractString;\n    format\n) -> Any\n\n\nSave the optimizer statistics to CSV or JSON\n\nArguments\n\nres::OptimizationProblemOutputs: Outputs\ndirectory::AbstractString : target directory\nformat = \"CSV\" : can be \"csv\" or \"json\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.export_optimizer_stats"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.export_realized_outputs-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.Outputs}","page":"Internals","text":"export_realized_outputs(\n    res::InfrastructureSystems.Outputs\n) -> String\n\n\nSave the realized outputs to CSV files for all variables, paramaters, duals, auxiliary variables, expressions, and optimizer statistics.\n\nArguments\n\nres::Outputs: Outputs\nsave_path::AbstractString : path to save outputs (defaults to simulation path)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.export_realized_outputs"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.find_key_with_value-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"find_key_with_value(d, value) -> Any\n\n\nReturn the key for the given value\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.find_key_with_value"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.find_timestamp_index-Tuple{Union{StepRange{Dates.DateTime, Dates.Millisecond}, Vector{Dates.DateTime}}, Dates.DateTime}","page":"Internals","text":"find_timestamp_index(\n    dates::Union{StepRange{Dates.DateTime, Dates.Millisecond}, Vector{Dates.DateTime}},\n    date::Dates.DateTime\n) -> Int64\n\n\ncalculates the index in the time series corresponding to the data. Assumes that the dates vector is sorted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.find_timestamp_index"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_bound-Tuple{LowerBound, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"get_bound(_::LowerBound, limits) -> Any\n\n\nExtract the relevant bound from a (min=, max=) NamedTuple.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_bound"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_column_names-Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Symbol, Any, OptimizationContainerKey}","page":"Internals","text":"get_column_names(\n    _::OptimizationContainer,\n    field::Symbol,\n    subcontainer,\n    key::OptimizationContainerKey\n) -> Any\n\n\nGet the column names for the specified container in the OptimizationContainer.\n\nArguments\n\ncontainer::OptimizationContainer: The optimization container.\nfield::Symbol: The field for which to retrieve the column names.\nkey::OptimizationContainerKey: The key for which to retrieve the column names.\n\nReturns\n\nTuple: Tuple of Vector{String}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_column_names"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_column_names_from_key-Tuple{OptimizationContainerKey}","page":"Internals","text":"get_column_names_from_key(\n    key::OptimizationContainerKey\n) -> Tuple{Vector}\n\n\nReturn the column names from a key as a tuple of vector of strings. Only useful for 1d DenseAxisArrays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_column_names_from_key"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_default_attributes-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{Type{U}, Type{F}}} where {U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"get_default_attributes(\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    _::Type{F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n) -> Dict{String, Any}\n\n\nExtension point: Get default attributes for a device formulation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_default_attributes"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_default_time_series_names-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{Type{U}, Type{F}}} where {U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"get_default_time_series_names(\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    _::Type{F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n) -> Dict{Type{<:ParameterType}, String}\n\n\nExtension point: Get default time series names for a device formulation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_default_time_series_names"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_enum_value-Tuple{Any, String}","page":"Internals","text":"get_enum_value(enum, value::String) -> Any\n\n\nGet the enum value for the string. Case insensitive.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_enum_value"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_forecast_horizon","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: forecast horizon configured on the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_forecast_horizon"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_forecast_interval","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: forecast interval configured on the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_forecast_interval"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_forecast_summary_table","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: summary table of forecasts on the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_forecast_summary_table"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_initial_input","page":"Internals","text":"get_initial_input(direction, device)\n\nReturn the initial_input scalar (cost at minimum) from the direction's side of the offer curve. POM provides methods dispatching on PSY.StaticInjection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_initial_input"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_last_updated_timestamp-Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DatasetContainer, OptimizationContainerKey}","page":"Internals","text":"get_last_updated_timestamp(\n    container::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DatasetContainer,\n    key::OptimizationContainerKey\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nReturn the timestamp from most recent data row updated in the dataset. This value may not be the same as the result from get_update_timestamp\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_last_updated_timestamp"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_last_updated_timestamp-Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HDF5Dataset}","page":"Internals","text":"get_last_updated_timestamp(\n    s::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HDF5Dataset\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nReturn the timestamp from most recent data row updated in the dataset. This value may not be the same as the result from get_update_timestamp\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_last_updated_timestamp"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_last_updated_timestamp-Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InMemoryDataset}","page":"Internals","text":"get_last_updated_timestamp(\n    s::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.InMemoryDataset\n) -> Dates.DateTime\n\n\nReturn the timestamp from most recent data row updated in the dataset. This value may not be the same as the result from get_update_timestamp\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_last_updated_timestamp"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_offer_curves","page":"Internals","text":"get_offer_curves(direction, device_or_cost)\n\nReturn the output/input offer curve(s) for the given direction. POM provides methods dispatching on PSY.StaticInjection and PSY.OfferCurveCost.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_offer_curves"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_param_eltype-Tuple{OptimizationContainer}","page":"Internals","text":"get_param_eltype(\n    container::OptimizationContainer\n) -> Union{Type{Float64}, Type{JuMP.VariableRef}}\n\n\nDetermine the element type for parameter arrays: JuMP.VariableRef for recurrent solves, Float64 otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_param_eltype"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_piecewise_curve_per_system_unit-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseStepData, InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem, Float64, Float64}","page":"Internals","text":"get_piecewise_curve_per_system_unit(\n    cost_component::InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseStepData,\n    unit_system::InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem,\n    system_base_power::Float64,\n    device_base_power::Float64\n) -> InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseStepData\n\n\nPiecewiseStepData normalized to system base. x-coords rescale as power values; y-coords are $ per unit of x and rescale by the inverse ratio.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_piecewise_curve_per_system_unit"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_piecewise_pointcurve_per_system_unit-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseLinearData, InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem, Float64, Float64}","page":"Internals","text":"get_piecewise_pointcurve_per_system_unit(\n    cost_component::InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseLinearData,\n    unit_system::InfrastructureSystems.RelativeUnits.AbstractUnitSystem,\n    system_base_power::Float64,\n    device_base_power::Float64\n) -> InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseLinearData\n\n\nPiecewiseLinearData normalized to system base. x-coords (power) rescale as power values; y-coords (/h) are invariant under power-base changes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_piecewise_pointcurve_per_system_unit"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_subsystem_components","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: get components of type T in a subsystem of the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_subsystem_components"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_system_uuid","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: stable UUID for the system (used as a filename identifier).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_system_uuid"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_counts","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: counts summary of time series on the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_counts"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_counts_by_type","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: counts by component type of time series on the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_counts_by_type"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_name-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{T, U, DeviceModelForBranches{U, F}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.TimeSeriesParameter, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"get_time_series_name(\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.TimeSeriesParameter,\n    d::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    model::DeviceModel{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n) -> String\n\n\nExtension point: Get default time series name for a parameter type. Returns the name of the time series to look for in the component.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_name"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_resolutions","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: time-series resolutions available on the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_time_series_resolutions"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_update_timestamp-Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractDataset}","page":"Internals","text":"get_update_timestamp(\n    s::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.AbstractDataset\n) -> Any\n\n\nReturn the timestamp from the data used in the last update\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_update_timestamp"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_update_timestamp-Tuple{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DatasetContainer, OptimizationContainerKey}","page":"Internals","text":"get_update_timestamp(\n    container::InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DatasetContainer,\n    key::OptimizationContainerKey\n) -> Any\n\n\nReturn the timestamp from the data used in the last update\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_update_timestamp"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_binary-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{U}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{T}, Type{U}, Type{F}}} where {T<:VariableType, U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, F<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}","page":"Internals","text":"get_variable_binary(\n    _::Type{T<:VariableType},\n    _::Type{U<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    _::Type{F<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Is the variable binary/integer?\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_binary"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_cost","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: read the primary variable cost from an operation-cost object. POM provides methods (typically delegating to PSY.get_variable).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_lower_bound-Tuple{Type{<:VariableType}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, Type{<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}}","page":"Internals","text":"get_variable_lower_bound(\n    _::Type{<:VariableType},\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    _::Type{<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Get variable lower bound.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_lower_bound"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_upper_bound-Tuple{Type{<:VariableType}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, Type{<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}}","page":"Internals","text":"get_variable_upper_bound(\n    _::Type{<:VariableType},\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    _::Type{<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Get variable upper bound.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_upper_bound"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_warm_start_value-Tuple{Type{<:VariableType}, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, Type{<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}}","page":"Internals","text":"get_variable_warm_start_value(\n    _::Type{<:VariableType},\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    _::Type{<:Union{InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation, InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractServiceFormulation}}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Get variable warm start value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.get_variable_warm_start_value"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.instantiate_network_model!-Tuple{AbstractOptimizationModel}","page":"Internals","text":"instantiate_network_model!(model::AbstractOptimizationModel)\n\n\nInstantiate the template's network model from the template's branch and service models.\n\nDownstream packages implement instantiate_network_model!(network_model, branch_models, service_models, number_of_steps, sys) per network formulation. Service models take part because a service defined over network elements can require the network setup to preserve them (for example, the branches a service is defined over must survive a network reduction).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.instantiate_network_model!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_nontrivial_offer-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseIncrementalCurve}}","page":"Internals","text":"is_nontrivial_offer(\n    curve::InfrastructureSystems.CostCurve{InfrastructureSystems.PiecewiseIncrementalCurve}\n) -> Bool\n\n\nIs this offer curve carrying meaningful data, as opposed to the default ZERO_OFFER_CURVE placeholder that PSY assigns to unused sides of a MarketBidCost / ImportExportCost? Only used for load formulations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_nontrivial_offer"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_nontrivial_offer-Tuple{OptimizationContainer, InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"is_nontrivial_offer(\n    _::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    curve\n) -> Bool\n\n\nis_nontrivial_offer(container, component, curve)\n\nBuild-context form of the predicate: does this offer side carry any quantity? A caller holding the component and container can resolve a time-series-backed side and test the quantity it actually offers, instead of inferring presence from the key alone. Use this form wherever both are in scope; the one-argument methods above answer from the key.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_nontrivial_offer"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_time_variant_proportional-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter}","page":"Internals","text":"is_time_variant_proportional(\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter\n) -> Bool\n\n\nExtension point: Check if proportional cost term is time-variant. Returns true if the cost should be added to the variant objective expression.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.is_time_variant_proportional"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.lookup_additional_axes-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"lookup_additional_axes(parameter_array) -> Any\n\n\nGiven a parameter array, return any additional axes, i.e. those that aren't the first (component) or the last (time).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.lookup_additional_axes"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.make_system_dirname-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer}","page":"Internals","text":"make_system_dirname(\n    sys::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsContainer\n)\n\n\nName of the serialized-system bundle written beside an outputs directory. A bundle is a directory (document plus time-series sidecar), not a single file, so this carries no extension.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.make_system_dirname"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.proportional_cost-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{O}, Tuple{O, Type{V}, C, Type{F}}} where {O<:InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter, V<:VariableType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"proportional_cost(\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter,\n    _::Type{V<:VariableType},\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    _::Type{F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Get proportional cost term from operation cost data. Non-time-varying signature - returns a single cost value for all time steps.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.proportional_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.proportional_cost-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{C}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{O}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, O, Type{V}, C, Type{F}, Int64}} where {O<:InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter, V<:VariableType, C<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"proportional_cost(\n    _::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.DeviceParameter,\n    _::Type{V<:VariableType},\n    _::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    _::Type{F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation},\n    _::Int64\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Get proportional cost term from operation cost data. Time-varying signature - may return different values per time step.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.proportional_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_json-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"read_json(\n    filename::AbstractString\n) -> Union{Nothing, Bool, Float64, Int64, String, JSON3.Array, JSON3.Object}\n\n\nReturn a decoded JSON file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.read_json"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.serialize_jump_optimization_model-Tuple{JuMP.Model, String}","page":"Internals","text":"serialize_jump_optimization_model(\n    jump_model::JuMP.Model,\n    save_path::String\n)\n\n\nExports the JuMP object in MathOptFormat\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.serialize_jump_optimization_model"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_expression!-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{S}, Tuple{OptimizationContainer, Type{S}, JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar, T, Int64}} where {S<:CostExpressions, T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Internals","text":"set_expression!(\n    container::OptimizationContainer,\n    _::Type{S<:CostExpressions},\n    cost_expression::JuMP.AbstractJuMPScalar,\n    component::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent,\n    time_period::Int64\n)\n\n\nReplaces an expression value in the expression container if the key exists\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.set_expression!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.skip_proportional_cost-Tuple{InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent}","page":"Internals","text":"skip_proportional_cost(\n    d::InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent\n) -> Bool\n\n\nExtension point: whether to skip adding proportional cost for a given device.\n\nFor thermals, equivalent to get_must_run, but that implementation belongs in POM.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.skip_proportional_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.sparse_variable_key_type-Tuple{Type{<:SparseVariableType}}","page":"Internals","text":"sparse_variable_key_type(\n    _::Type{<:SparseVariableType}\n) -> Type{Tuple{String, Int64, Int64}}\n\n\nKey tuple type for the empty SparseAxisArray auto-created for a SparseVariableType.\n\nDefaults to the 3D device-offer PWL shape (device_name, segment, time). A variable type that needs an extra axis - e.g. a per-service reserve offer keyed (service_name, device_name, segment, time) - overrides this method to widen the key. Downstream packages extend it for their own sparse variable types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.sparse_variable_key_type"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.start_up_cost-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{V}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{Any, Type{T}, Type{V}, Type{F}}} where {T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent, V<:VariableType, F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}","page":"Internals","text":"start_up_cost(\n    cost,\n    _::Type{T<:InfrastructureSystems.InfrastructureSystemsComponent},\n    _::Type{V<:VariableType},\n    _::Type{F<:InfrastructureSystems.Optimization.AbstractDeviceFormulation}\n)\n\n\nExtension point: Convert raw startup cost to a scalar value. Device-specific implementations (e.g., for StartUpStages, MultiStartVariable) are in POM.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.start_up_cost"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_dataframe-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{T, 2, Ax, L} where {Ax, L<:Tuple{JuMP.Containers._AxisLookup, JuMP.Containers._AxisLookup}}, OptimizationContainerKey}} where T<:Union{Number, Tuple{Vararg{Number}}, Vector{<:Tuple{Number, Number}}}","page":"Internals","text":"to_dataframe(\n    array::JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray{T<:Union{Number, Tuple{Vararg{Number}}, Vector{<:Tuple{Number, Number}}}, 2, Ax, L} where {Ax, L<:Tuple{JuMP.Containers._AxisLookup, JuMP.Containers._AxisLookup}},\n    key::OptimizationContainerKey\n) -> DataFrame\n\n\nCreate a DataFrame from a JuMP DenseAxisArray or SparseAxisArray.\n\nArguments\n\narray: JuMP DenseAxisArray or SparseAxisArray to convert\nkey::OptimizationContainerKey:\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_dataframe"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_matrix-Tuple{T} where T<:OptimizerStats","page":"Internals","text":"to_matrix(stats::OptimizerStats) -> Matrix{Float64}\n\n\nConvert OptimizerStats to a matrix of floats that can be serialized.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_matrix-Tuple{Vector}","page":"Internals","text":"to_matrix(vec::Vector) -> Matrix\n\n\nConvert Vectors, DenseAxisArrays, and SparkAxisArrays to a matrix.\n\nIf the input is a 1d array or DenseAxisArray, the returned matrix will have a number of rows equal to the length of the input and one column.\nIf the input is a 2d DenseAxisArray, the dimensions are transposed, due to the way we store outputs in JuMP.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_matrix"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_outputs_dataframe-Tuple{JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"to_outputs_dataframe(\n    array::JuMP.Containers.DenseAxisArray,\n    timestamps\n) -> Any\n\n\nConvert a DenseAxisArray containing components to a outputs DataFrame consumable by users.\n\nArguments\n\narray: DenseAxisArray: JuMP DenseAxisArray to convert\ntimestamps: Iterable of timestamps for each component or nothing if time is not known. The resulting DataFrame will have the column \"DateTime\" if timestamps is not nothing. Otherwise, it will have the column \"time_index\", representing the index of the time dimension.\n::Val{TableFormat}: Format of the table to create. If it is TableFormat.LONG, the DataFrame will have the column \"name\", and, if the data has three dimensions, \"name2.\" If it is TableFormat.WIDE, the DataFrame will have columns for each component. Wide format does not support arrays with more than two dimensions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.to_outputs_dataframe"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(::Type{<:QuadraticApproxConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest depth L whose worst-case approximation error on a domain of length max_delta = Δ is ≤ tolerance. Each concrete config implements this method with its own depth-to-error formula.\n\nEvery config's worst-case error has the form Δ²·c(L), where c(L) is the method's unit-domain error coefficient (Sawtooth: 2^{-2L-2}, NMDT: 2^{-L-2}, DNMDT: 2^{-2L-2}, SOS2: 1/(4·L²), Epigraph: 2^{-2L-4}, …). The Δ² prefactor comes from unnormalization: each method normalizes x = a + Δ·xh with xh ∈ [0, 1], approximates the only nonlinear term Δ²·xh² in x² = a² + 2a·Δ·xh + Δ²·xh², and inherits the unit-domain error scaled by Δ².\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTBilinearConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta_x,\n    max_delta_y\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{DNMDTBilinearConfig}; tolerance, max_delta_x, max_delta_y)::Int\n\nSmallest DNMDT bilinear depth L whose worst-case relaxation gap on [ax, ax+Δx] × [ay, ay+Δy] falls within tolerance. Inverts Δx·Δy·2^{-2L-2} ≤ τ:\n\nL = ⌈(log₂(Δx·Δy/τ) − 2) / 2⌉\n\nclamped to L ≥ 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{DNMDTQuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest DNMDT depth L whose worst-case overestimation gap on [a, a+Δ] falls within tolerance. Inverts Δ²·2^{-2L-2} ≤ τ:\n\nL = ⌈(log₂(Δ²/τ) − 2) / 2⌉\n\nclamped to L ≥ 1. Sizes only the DNMDT side.\n\nContract on epigraph_depth: the returned depth meets the tolerance iff the user picks epigraph_depth = 0 (tightening disabled) or epigraph_depth ≥ depth − 1. The DNMDT side error is Δ²·2^{-2L-2} and the epigraph side error is Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4}; epigraph ≤ DNMDT iff L_e ≥ L − 1. When 0 < epigraph_depth < depth − 1, the epigraph side has a larger error than the DNMDT side and the realized error can exceed tolerance. Use tolerance_epigraph_depth to size both knobs consistently.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphQuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.EpigraphQuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{EpigraphQuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest epigraph depth L whose worst-case underestimation gap on [a, a+Δ] falls within tolerance. Inverts the closed-form bound Δ²·2^{-2L-4} ≤ τ:\n\nL = ⌈(log₂(Δ²/τ) − 4) / 2⌉\n\nclamped to L ≥ 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{ManualSOS2QuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest SOS2 segment count d whose worst-case PWL gap on [a, a+Δ] falls within tolerance. Inverts Δ²/(4·d²) ≤ τ:\n\nd = ⌈Δ / (2·√τ)⌉\n\nclamped to d ≥ 1. pwmcc_segments does not enter the error bound, so it is left to the constructor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTBilinearConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta_x,\n    max_delta_y\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{NMDTBilinearConfig}; tolerance, max_delta_x, max_delta_y)::Int\n\nSmallest NMDT bilinear depth L whose worst-case relaxation gap on [ax, ax+Δx] × [ay, ay+Δy] falls within tolerance. Inverts Δx·Δy·2^{-L-2} ≤ τ:\n\nL = ⌈log₂(Δx·Δy/τ) − 2⌉\n\nclamped to L ≥ 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{NMDTQuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest NMDT depth L whose worst-case overestimation gap on [a, a+Δ] falls within tolerance. Inverts Δ²·2^{-L-2} ≤ τ:\n\nL = ⌈log₂(Δ²/τ) − 2⌉\n\nclamped to L ≥ 1. Sizes only the NMDT side.\n\nContract on epigraph_depth: the returned depth meets the tolerance iff the user picks epigraph_depth = 0 (tightening disabled) or epigraph_depth ≥ ⌈(depth − 2) / 2⌉. The NMDT side error is Δ²·2^{-L-2} and the epigraph side error is Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4}; epigraph ≤ NMDT iff 2L_e + 4 ≥ L + 2, i.e. L_e ≥ (L − 2)/2. When the user picks a smaller epigraph_depth, the epigraph side has a larger error than the NMDT side and the realized error can exceed tolerance. Use tolerance_epigraph_depth to size both knobs consistently.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{SawtoothQuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest sawtooth depth L whose worst-case overestimation gap on [a, a+Δ] falls within tolerance. Inverts the closed-form bound Δ²·2^{-2L-2} ≤ τ:\n\nL = ⌈(log₂(Δ²/τ) − 2) / 2⌉\n\nclamped to L ≥ 1. Sizes only the sawtooth side of the formulation.\n\nContract on epigraph_depth: the returned depth meets the tolerance iff the user picks epigraph_depth = 0 (tightening disabled) or epigraph_depth ≥ depth − 1. When 0 < epigraph_depth < depth − 1, the epigraph side of the sandwich has a larger error than the sawtooth side (epigraph Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4} vs sawtooth Δ²·2^{-2L-2}), and since result_expr is free in [epigraph(x), sawtooth(x)] in larger optimization contexts the realized error can exceed tolerance. Use tolerance_epigraph_depth below to size both knobs consistently.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{SolverSOS2QuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest SOS2 segment count d whose worst-case PWL gap on [a, a+Δ] falls within tolerance. Inverts Δ²/(4·d²) ≤ τ:\n\nd = ⌈Δ / (2·√τ)⌉\n\nclamped to d ≥ 1. pwmcc_segments does not enter the error bound, so it is left to the constructor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Union{Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config{Q}}}, Tuple{Q}} where Q<:Union{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.Bin2Config{Q<:Union{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig}}};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta_x,\n    max_delta_y\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{Bin2Config{Q}}; tolerance, max_delta_x, max_delta_y)::Int\n\nInner-quad depth such that Bin2's worst-case gap |z − xy| is ≤ tolerance. Derivation: see the comment block above.\n\nFor one-sided-over inner quads (SawtoothQuadConfig, SolverSOS2QuadConfig, ManualSOS2QuadConfig), forwards to tolerance_depth(Q; tolerance = 2·τ, max_delta = Δx + Δy).\n\nFor two-sided inner quads (NMDTQuadConfig, DNMDTQuadConfig), forwards to tolerance_depth(Q; tolerance = (Δx+Δy)²·τ/(Δx² + Δy² + Δx·Δy), max_delta = Δx + Δy).\n\nEpigraphQuadConfig is excluded. The epigraph is one-sided-under (z• ≤ •²), so with εx = x² − zx ≥ 0 and εy = y² − zy ≥ 0 (unbounded above in the LP relaxation, since the LP imposes no lower-side gap on zx, zy) and εp = (x+y)² − z_p ≥ 0:\n\nz − xy = ½(z_p − z_x − z_y) − xy\n      = ½((x+y)² − ε_p − (x² − ε_x) − (y² − ε_y)) − xy\n      = ½(2xy − ε_p + ε_x + ε_y) − xy\n      = ½(ε_x + ε_y − ε_p).\n\nIn the LP relaxation εx and εy have no finite upper bound (an LP solver can drive zx and zy as low as the variable bounds allow), so z − xy can be made arbitrarily large. No finite tolerance_depth recovers a bound. This rules out epigraph as an inner Q for Bin2.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth-Union{Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig{Q}}}, Tuple{Q}} where Q<:Union{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig{Q<:Union{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig}}};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta_x,\n    max_delta_y\n)\n\n\ntolerance_depth(::Type{HybSConfig{Q}}; tolerance, max_delta_x, max_delta_y)::Int\n\nInner-quad depth for HybS at target tolerance τ. Returns the smallest depth whose inner-quad error on [ax, ax+Δx] (and [ay, ay+Δy]) is ≤ τ/2, which satisfies the ε_Q ≤ τ/2 half of the HybS budget.\n\nDefined only for strictly one-sided-over inner quads: SawtoothQuadConfig, SolverSOS2QuadConfig, ManualSOS2QuadConfig. Other Q raise MethodError. See the HybSConfig docstring for why two-sided or one-sided-under inner Qs (EpigraphQuadConfig, NMDTQuadConfig, DNMDTQuadConfig) make the sandwich infeasible.\n\nSee also tolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{HybSConfig{Q}}; …) for the second knob.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_epigraph_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.DNMDTQuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{DNMDTQuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest epigraph_depth whose epigraph error on [a, a+Δ] is ≤ tolerance. Pass alongside tolerance_depth(DNMDTQuadConfig; …) to honor the contract.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_epigraph_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.NMDTQuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{NMDTQuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest epigraph_depth whose epigraph error on [a, a+Δ] is ≤ tolerance. Pass alongside tolerance_depth(NMDTQuadConfig; …) to honor the contract.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth-Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig}}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_epigraph_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta\n)\n\n\ntolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{SawtoothQuadConfig}; tolerance, max_delta)::Int\n\nSmallest epigraph_depth consistent with tolerance_depth(SawtoothQuadConfig; …) under target tolerance τ. Returns the depth at which the epigraph (LP lower) side of the sandwich has worst-case error ≤ τ on [a, a+Δ]. Since the epigraph's per-unit error is Δ²·2^{-2L_e-4} versus the sawtooth's Δ²·2^{-2L-2}, this is one less than the sawtooth depth for the same tolerance — which exactly meets the contract epigraph_depth ≥ depth − 1.\n\nOptional: callers that want to disable epigraph tightening can pass epigraph_depth = 0 and the sawtooth-side bound still holds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth-Union{Tuple{Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig{Q}}}, Tuple{Q}} where Q<:Union{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig}","page":"Internals","text":"tolerance_epigraph_depth(\n    ::Type{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.HybSConfig{Q<:Union{InfrastructureOptimizationModels.ManualSOS2QuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SawtoothQuadConfig, InfrastructureOptimizationModels.SolverSOS2QuadConfig}}};\n    tolerance,\n    max_delta_x,\n    max_delta_y\n)\n\n\ntolerance_epigraph_depth(::Type{HybSConfig{Q}}; tolerance, max_delta_x, max_delta_y)::Int\n\nEpigraph depth for HybS at target tolerance τ. Returns the smallest depth whose epigraph error on the cross-term range Δx + Δy is ≤ τ, which satisfies the ½ε_E ≤ τ/2 half of the HybS budget.\n\nDefined only for strictly one-sided-over inner quads: SawtoothQuadConfig, SolverSOS2QuadConfig, ManualSOS2QuadConfig. Other Q raise MethodError.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.tolerance_epigraph_depth"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.transform_single_time_series!","page":"Internals","text":"Extension point: transform single time series into deterministic forecasts on the system.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.transform_single_time_series!"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.validate_occ_breakpoints_slopes","page":"Internals","text":"validate_occ_breakpoints_slopes(device, direction)\n\nValidate breakpoints/slopes on the given direction's offer curve.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.validate_occ_breakpoints_slopes"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/internal/#InfrastructureOptimizationModels.validate_occ_component","page":"Internals","text":"validate_occ_component(::Type{<:ParameterType}, device)\n\nValidate that device can be processed by the given offer-curve-cost parameter. POM provides overloads per device type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"InfrastructureOptimizationModels.validate_occ_component"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/generated_stub/","page":"-","text":"Please refer to the Tutorial section of the diataxis framework. Unlike the other documentation sections, Tutorials are written as scripts, then automatically processed into markdown files and Jupyter notebooks using the Literate.jl package. This functionality is implemented in make_tutorials.jl.","title":"-"}]
